   "concept": "The Koebner (isomorphic) phenomenon is the development of lesions of an existing dermatosis at sites of trauma such as a scratch, scar or surgical wound, appearing along the line of injury; it is characteristically seen in psoriasis, lichen planus, vitiligo and viral warts. The Nikolsky sign (epidermal shearing) belongs to pemphigus, Darier sign (wheal on rubbing) to mastocytosis, and Auspitz sign (pinpoint bleeding on scale removal) to psoriatic scale, so Koebner is the correct term for the response described.",
