   "topic": "Asphyxial deaths (hanging, drowning)",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A man dives into very cold water and dies almost instantly, before any water can be aspirated; autopsy shows none of the usual signs of drowning. This 'immersion syndrome' (hydrocution) is best explained by:",
