   "subject": "Forensic Medicine (FMT)",
   "topic": "Death, postmortem changes (rigor/livor/algor)",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Molecular (cellular) death, as distinct from somatic death, is best defined as which of the following?",
   "options": [
    "The irreversible stoppage of the functions of the brain, heart and lungs together",
    "The death of individual cells and tissues, occurring a few hours after somatic death",
    "The point at which the electroencephalogram first becomes isoelectric",
