   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Somatic death is the irreversible cessation of the three interdependent systems — nervous, circulatory and respiratory. Molecular or cellular death follows it: individual cells and tissues survive briefly and die gradually, roughly 3-4 hours after somatic death, as their oxygen supply ceases. This residual cellular life is what allows tissues such as cornea and skin to be harvested for a short while after death. Option A actually defines somatic death, not molecular death.",
