    "The central nervous system (brain)",
    "The circulatory system (heart)",
    "The renal excretory system (kidneys)"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "In Bichat's classical grouping, the mode of death names which of the three vital systems fails first. Coma is death from primary failure of the brain (nervous system), syncope is death from sudden and complete failure of the heart's action (circulation), and asphyxia is death from primary failure of respiration and oxygenation. Syncope may follow massive haemorrhage, a cardiac arrhythmia or vagal inhibition. The kidney is not one of Bichat's three modes.",
