   "concept": "The rate of cooling rises with the ratio of body surface area to mass and with the temperature gradient to the surroundings. A thin infant has a very high surface-area-to-mass ratio, little insulating fat, no clothing, and lies on a cold conducting surface, so it cools fastest. Obesity, clothing or blankets, a warm environment, and a febrile state (a raised temperature at the moment of death) all slow apparent cooling. Hence the emaciated unclothed infant on cold stone cools most quickly.",
