   "concept": "Tardieu spots are pin-point (about 0.1-0.5 mm) petechial haemorrhages that appear in the most dependent, deeply congested parts of a body, particularly where hypostasis is intense and where death was associated with asphyxia. They result from the raised intravascular pressure of pooled, settling blood rupturing small distended capillaries and venules. They are a postmortem phenomenon and should not be misread as evidence of antemortem injury or of disease.",
