   "concept": "The stomach normally begins to empty soon after eating and is largely empty within a few hours (a light meal in about 2 hours, a full meal in about 4-6 hours). A stomach full of recently ingested, recognisable and undigested food therefore indicates death within roughly one to two hours of the last meal, and the nature of the food may itself help identify the meal. Because gastric emptying is affected by illness, emotion, drugs and the type of meal, this estimate of time since the last meal is only a rough guide and must be corroborated.",
