   "topic": "Mycobacteria (TB, leprosy) & lab diagnosis",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Mycobacterium tuberculosis shows a marked predilection for the apices of the lungs and grows preferentially in the upper part of a Lowenstein-Jensen slant. This behaviour is best explained by the fact that the organism is:",
