   "topic": "Glaucoma",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A 4-month-old infant is brought with persistent watering, marked intolerance to light and squeezing of the eyelids; both corneas appear enlarged and hazy. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
