    "Overestimate the true IOP",
    "Measure the true IOP exactly",
    "Be completely unaffected by corneal thickness"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Goldmann tonometry is calibrated for an average central corneal thickness of about 520-545 microns. A thin cornea offers less resistance to applanation, so the measured pressure reads lower than the true IOP (underestimation) — an important reason why thin-cornea ocular hypertensives progress and are under-treated. A thick cornea causes overestimation. This is why pachymetry is part of every glaucoma work-up, especially after LASIK.",
   "reference": "Parsons' Diseases of the Eye 23e, Ch. Tonometry and central corneal thickness",
   "verified": "Y",
