   "topic": "Glaucoma",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A 68-year-old with open-angle glaucoma shows, on slit-lamp examination, greyish-white flaky dandruff-like deposits on the anterior lens capsule in a target pattern and along the pupillary margin. The most likely diagnosis is:",
