   "concept": "Pseudoexfoliation syndrome deposits fibrillar grey-white basement-membrane-like material on the anterior lens capsule (a central disc plus a peripheral band separated by a clear zone), the pupil margin, zonules and trabecular meshwork; meshwork obstruction raises IOP. It is the commonest identifiable cause of secondary open-angle glaucoma, is often asymmetric, is associated with weak zonules (cataract-surgery risk) and produces higher, more resistant IOP spikes than POAG.",
