   "stem": "A 60-year-old has glaucomatous optic disc cupping and arcuate field loss, but repeated readings show IOP of 14-16 mmHg with open angles and a normal central corneal thickness; the disc shows a splinter haemorrhage at its margin. The most likely diagnosis is:",
