   "subject": "Ophthalmology",
   "topic": "Refractive errors",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A soft contact lens wearer who habitually sleeps in her lenses presents with a painful red eye, photophobia, and a corneal stromal infiltrate with an overlying epithelial defect. The most sight-threatening diagnosis is:",
   "options": [
    "Giant papillary conjunctivitis",
    "Microbial (bacterial) keratitis",
    "Contact-lens-induced dry eye",
    "Corneal neovascularisation"
   ],
