   "topic": "Refractive errors",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "An adult with +1.00 D hypermetropia in the right eye and +6.00 D in the left develops troublesome asthenopia and a difference in the size of the two retinal images when wearing spectacles. The optical correction that best minimises this aniseikonia is:",
