   "topic": "Acute & chronic inflammation, healing/repair",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A patient with aspirin-exacerbated respiratory disease develops bronchospasm after taking aspirin, because cyclooxygenase inhibition shunts arachidonic acid toward the lipoxygenase pathway. Which drug directly inhibits the 5-lipoxygenase ENZYME (rather than the leukotriene receptor)?",
   "options": [
