   "subject": "Pathology",
   "topic": "Acute & chronic inflammation, healing/repair",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A boy has recurrent infections with catalase-positive organisms (Staphylococcus aureus, Aspergillus, Serratia, Burkholderia) and forms granulomas; a dihydrorhodamine (DHR) flow-cytometry test is abnormal. The defective process is:",
   "options": [
