   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Which subtype of classical Hodgkin lymphoma is most strongly associated with Epstein-Barr virus, is more common in older adults, HIV-positive patients and developing countries, and shows numerous classic Reed-Sternberg cells in a mixed inflammatory background of eosinophils, plasma cells and histiocytes?",
   "options": [
    "Nodular sclerosis",
    "Nodular lymphocyte-predominant",
    "Lymphocyte-rich",
    "Mixed cellularity"
