   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Assertion (A): Contraction band necrosis is a hallmark of reperfusion injury after blood flow is restored to ischemic myocardium. Reason (R): Reperfusion causes massive calcium influx into irreversibly injured myocytes, producing hypercontracted sarcomeres seen as intensely eosinophilic transverse bands.",
