   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Assertion (A): Hepatitis D superinfection of a chronic hepatitis B carrier tends to be more severe — with higher risk of fulminant hepatitis or accelerated cirrhosis — than simultaneous HBV-HDV coinfection. Reason (R): Hepatitis D is a defective RNA virus that requires the HBsAg coat of hepatitis B to replicate.",
