   "subject": "Pharmacology",
   "topic": "General & local anaesthetics, opioids",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Ketamine is generally avoided in a patient with raised intracranial pressure or an open-globe (penetrating) eye injury because it:",
   "options": [
    "Causes profound systemic hypotension",
    "Increases cerebral blood flow, intracranial pressure and intra-ocular pressure",
