   "topic": "General & local anaesthetics, opioids",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Assertion (A): Atracurium is a suitable neuromuscular blocker in a patient with combined severe hepatic and renal failure. Reason (R): Atracurium is eliminated by Hofmann degradation, a process independent of hepatic and renal function. Select the correct option.",
   "options": [
