   "id": "Q_GEN_PHAR_CNS_ANES_016",
   "subject": "Pharmacology",
   "topic": "General & local anaesthetics, opioids",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "At the end of surgery, residual non-depolarizing neuromuscular block is reversed with neostigmine. Neostigmine is deliberately co-administered with glycopyrrolate (or atropine) in order to:",
   "options": [
    "Potentiate the neuromuscular blockade",
