   "concept": "Adenosine is the drug of choice for acute termination of AV-nodal reentrant supraventricular tachycardia. Given as a rapid IV bolus, it activates A1 receptors, opening potassium channels and inhibiting calcium current in the AV node, transiently blocking AV conduction and interrupting the reentry circuit. Its half-life is only a few seconds, so effects (flushing, chest tightness, transient asystole) are brief. Lidocaine (A) is for ventricular arrhythmias, digoxin (C) is too slow for acute conversion, and quinidine (D) is not used here. Effects are potentiated by dipyridamole and blocked by methylxanthines.",
