   "concept": "Secondary attack rate (SAR) = number of exposed contacts developing disease within one incubation period divided by the total number of SUSCEPTIBLE contacts exposed to the primary case, times 100. It measures infectiousness/communicability and the impact of interventions within closed groups such as households. Option A gives an overall community attack/incidence rate, not SAR; primary cases (B) and all cumulative infections (D) are not the correct denominator. Immune contacts are excluded from the denominator, since only susceptibles are at risk of becoming secondary cases.",
