   "concept": "ARTI (Annual Risk of Tuberculosis Infection) is the probability of acquiring new TB infection in one year; it is estimated INDIRECTLY from tuberculin (Mantoux) surveys in children (the prevalence of infection is converted into an annual risk) and is a sensitive index of the trend of TB transmission in the community. It is not derived from sputum microscopy (option A) or drug-resistance data (option D), and a FALLING — not rising — ARTI indicates programme success (option C is wrong). Historically about a 1% ARTI corresponded to a substantial smear-positive case load.",
