   "concept": "Primaquine, an 8-aminoquinoline, is given for its public-health / transmission-control value: it kills the dormant liver hypnozoites of P. vivax (and P. ovale), preventing relapses (radical cure), and it is gametocytocidal against P. falciparum, reducing onward transmission to mosquitoes. It is NOT the rapid blood schizonticide for the acute attack (that role belongs to chloroquine or ACT, so option A is wrong), it is not durable prophylaxis (option B), and it does not affect chloroquine resistance (option C). G6PD status must be checked, as primaquine can precipitate haemolysis.",
