   "concept": "Under the WHO/India multi-dose Open Vial Policy, opened vials of OPV, DPT, TT, DT, hepatitis B and liquid pentavalent (preservative-containing) may be reused for up to 28 days if storage and labelling conditions are met. However, RECONSTITUTED vaccines — BCG and measles/MR (and live JE) — must be discarded at the end of the session or within about 4 hours, whichever is earlier, because they contain no preservative and readily support contamination once reconstituted. The policy reduces vaccine wastage while protecting safety; verify specifics against current national cold-chain guidelines.",
