   "concept": "Circulating vaccine-derived poliovirus (cVDPV) results from prolonged person-to-person circulation of the live attenuated virus in ORAL polio vaccine (OPV) within under-immunised populations, allowing it to regain neurovirulence and transmissibility — hence it CAN cause paralysis (option C wrong) and IS driven by low population immunity (option D wrong). It does not arise from injectable IPV, which is killed (option A wrong). This risk is why the world is shifting from OPV toward IPV; India uses IPV in the schedule alongside pulse polio campaigns, and cVDPV surveillance is central to the polio endgame strategy.",
