   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "topic": "Demography, family planning, MCH indicators",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Assertion (A): The crude death rate is not a satisfactory measure for comparing mortality between two different countries. Reason (R): The crude death rate is strongly influenced by the age and sex composition of the population.",
   "options": [
