   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "The NPP 2000 set objectives on three horizons: the IMMEDIATE objective was to address unmet needs for contraception, health infrastructure and personnel; the MEDIUM-TERM objective was to bring the Total Fertility Rate down to replacement level (about 2.1) by 2010 through inter-sectoral operational strategies; and the LONG-TERM objective was to achieve a stable population by around 2045 at a level consistent with sustainable economic growth and social development. The policy is voluntary and target-free at the individual level, explicitly rejecting coercion (options B and C are wrong). Specific NPP targets/dates are change-prone policy facts — verify against the official document.",
