   "concept": "Sensitivity = TP / (TP + FN). Of the 150 diseased people, 135 test positive so TP = 135 and FN = 150 - 135 = 15; sensitivity = 135 / 150 = 0.90 = 90%. The 70 false positives among non-diseased people do not enter the sensitivity calculation, so the answer is C (90%).",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Screening for Disease",
