   "id": "Q_GEN_PSM_EPI_SCREEN_013",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "topic": "Screening: sensitivity/specificity/PPV",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Using the same data (500 people screened, 150 truly diseased, the test positive in 135 diseased persons and in 70 non-diseased persons), what is the specificity of the test?",
   "options": [
    "80%",
    "90%",
    "75%",
    "66%"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Non-diseased persons = 500 - 150 = 350. False positives = 70, so true negatives TN = 350 - 70 = 280. Specificity = TN / (TN + FP) = 280 / 350 = 0.80 = 80%. Diseased counts do not affect specificity, so the answer is A (80%).",
