   "concept": "LR+ = sensitivity / (1 - specificity) = 0.90 / (1 - 0.80) = 0.90 / 0.20 = 4.5. Option A (0.125) is instead the negative likelihood ratio LR- = (1 - 0.90) / 0.80 = 0.10 / 0.80. Options B and D do not follow from the formula, so the answer is C (4.5).",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Screening for Disease",
