   "concept": "Using the same table, true negatives TN = 1440 and false negatives FN = 20. NPV = TN / (TN + FN) = 1440 / (1440 + 20) = 1440 / 1460 = 0.986 = 98.6%. In low-prevalence settings the NPV stays high because very few diseased individuals exist to be missed, so the answer is D.",
