   "concept": "Lowering the cutoff labels more people positive, capturing more true cases so sensitivity rises, but it also generates more false positives so specificity falls, which is option C. Raising the cutoff reverses this. This unavoidable sensitivity-specificity trade-off is exactly what the ROC curve depicts. Prevalence is a population property unaffected by the cutoff.",
