   "concept": "Wilson and Jungner require an important, sufficiently common condition with a recognizable latent or early stage, a suitable acceptable and valid test, an accepted effective treatment, facilities for diagnosis and treatment, and a favourable cost balance. A rare, rapidly fatal disease with no detectable preclinical phase (very short sojourn time) is UNSUITABLE for screening, so D is NOT a criterion.",
