   "topic": "Schizophrenia & psychosis",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A patient has had prominent mood (manic and depressive) episodes for most of a 2-year illness, but there was also a clear 3-week period during which delusions and hallucinations persisted while mood symptoms were entirely absent. The diagnosis that best fits is:",
