   "subject": "Psychiatry",
   "topic": "Schizophrenia & psychosis",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Two weeks after starting an antipsychotic, a patient complains of an intolerable inner restlessness and cannot stop pacing or shifting his legs. Besides reducing the dose, the most appropriate pharmacological management is:",
