   "concept": "Protective lead aprons for diagnostic radiology provide 0.25 to 0.5 mm lead equivalence, with 0.5 mm preferred for higher-kVp and fluoroscopy work; this attenuates roughly 90 to 95 percent of scattered radiation at common diagnostic energies. Aprons are designed against scatter, not the primary beam, and must be inspected periodically for cracks. Thyroid shields and lead glasses further reduce organ dose.",
