   "concept": "A dying declaration is ideally recorded by a Magistrate, though where none is available a doctor or indeed any person may record it. No oath is administered, since the maxim nemo moriturus praesumitur mentiri assumes a dying person does not lie, and leading questions must be avoided so the words remain the declarant's own. Unlike English law, Indian law does not require the declarant to have been under expectation of death.",
