   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A 29-year-old woman presents with abdominal pain, vaginal bleeding and 6 weeks of amenorrhea. Transvaginal ultrasound shows neither an intrauterine gestational sac nor features of ectopic pregnancy. Her serum beta-hCG is 1,200 IU/L, below the discriminatory zone. What is the next step in management?",
