   "concept": "In a haemodynamically stable woman with a pregnancy of unknown location - serum beta-hCG below the discriminatory zone (~1500-2000 IU/L) and non-diagnostic ultrasound - the next step is to repeat serum beta-hCG in 48 hours; appropriate doubling suggests an intrauterine pregnancy, while a suboptimal rise/plateau suggests ectopic or failing pregnancy.",
   "reference": "FMGE January 2025 Part 1 (real exam recall); DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. Abortion and Ectopic Pregnancy",
