    "Hypocalcemia",
    "Hypokalemia",
    "Hyperkalemia"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Vomiting, diarrhoea and laxative abuse all cause gastrointestinal potassium loss; the resulting hypokalaemia is the electrolyte disturbance that precipitates cardiac arrhythmias. Hypocalcaemia prolongs the QT interval but is not the primary abnormality here.",
