   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A 68-year-old hypertensive man presents in acute distress, diaphoretic and hypotensive with severe chest pain, and his ECG shows a regular narrow-complex tachycardia at 150 per minute with saw-tooth atrial waves in the inferior leads. What is the most appropriate immediate management?",
   "options": [
