   "concept": "An untreated hyperthyroid patient taken to surgery without proper preoperative optimisation has heightened catecholamine sensitivity and risks tachyarrhythmias (and thyroid storm) intraoperatively; arrhythmia is the leading immediate danger. Adequate preop control with antithyroid drugs and beta-blockers is essential.",
