    "Wide bore needle in 2nd ICS",
    "Pericardiocentesis",
    "Pleurodesis with doxycycline"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Distended neck veins, absent breath sounds, hyperresonance and tracheal deviation away from the affected side are tension pneumothorax, a clinical diagnosis needing immediate needle decompression (wide-bore cannula in the 2nd intercostal space mid-clavicular line) before any imaging, followed by a chest tube. Waiting for a CXR can be fatal.",
