   "topic": "Anemias (micro/macro/hemolytic)",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A child with sickle cell disease already on hydroxyurea has persistent symptomatic haemolytic anaemia with a haemoglobin of 6.5 g/dL. Which agent directly inhibits haemoglobin S polymerisation to raise the haemoglobin?",
   "options": [
    "Hydroxyurea",
    "Azacytidine",
    "Voxelotor",
