   "topic": "Stroke, epilepsy, meningitis",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "What is the probable diagnosis in a patient with miosis, anhidrosis, mild ptosis and a persistently small pupil even in low light?",
   "options": [
    "Adie's tonic pupil",
    "Horner syndrome",
    "Marcus Gunn pupil",
    "Argyll Robertson pupil"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Miosis, mild ptosis (weak Muller muscle) and ipsilateral facial anhidrosis with a pupil that stays small in dim light is Horner syndrome, due to interruption of the ocular sympathetic pathway. Argyll Robertson pupils (neurosyphilis) are small but light-near dissociated, Adie's is a large tonic pupil, and Marcus Gunn is a relative afferent defect.",
