    "Displacement of endotracheal tube (ET)",
    "Air embolism",
    "Dislodgement of ET"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "The subclavian vein lies against the pleural dome, so a failed subclavian cannulation commonly causes pneumothorax; air in the pleural space reduces venous return, giving hypotension with reflex tachycardia and threatening a tension pneumothorax. Air embolism is possible but pneumothorax is the classic complication of this attempt.",
