   "topic": "Wounds, firearm & mechanical injuries",
   "part": "A",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "After a road traffic accident, NCCT head was normal on admission. The patient later died in the ICU following coma, and brain biopsy revealed multiple punctate haemorrhages. What is the diagnosis?",
   "options": [
    "Ischemic injury",
    "Diffuse axonal injury",
    "Intraventricular bleeding",
    "Subdural hemorrhage"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "A high-speed head injury with a normal initial CT but prolonged coma and multiple deep punctate white-matter haemorrhages is diffuse axonal injury, caused by shearing/rotational forces tearing axons in the white matter, corpus callosum and brainstem. Subdural bleeds are crescentic on CT and ischaemic infarcts give territorial hypodensity, not scattered petechiae.",
