   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "When immunocompetent donor lymphocytes are transferred into a recipient who cannot reject them (immunocompromised host), the donor T cells attack host tissues: graft-versus-host disease, giving systemic features (fever, rash, hepatitis, diarrhoea) plus sclerodermatous skin contractures. Host-versus-graft rejection requires an immunocompetent recipient, and graft failure/necrosis occurs early without systemic immune features.",
