   "concept": "Absence of the crystalline lens (aphakia, usually after cataract extraction without an IOL) removes about +15 D of refractive power, so a high-plus correction (roughly +10 to +12 D) is needed; the eye also shows a deep anterior chamber, iridodonesis and a jet-black pupil. A pseudophakic eye (with an IOL) needs little correction, and simple hypermetropia rarely needs more than +4 to +5 D.",
