   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Rising oestrogen in early puberty makes the vaginal epithelium proliferate and produce glycogen, which lactobacilli convert to lactic acid, giving a normal white, odourless physiological leukorrhoea. GnRH and inhibin B act on the pituitary/gonadal axis without directly producing this discharge (and 'B-Lynch suture' is a surgical technique - an erroneous distractor).",
