    "Suspensory (Cooper's) ligaments",
    "Pectoral fascia",
    "Subcutaneous fat"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Malignant infiltration and fibrosis shorten the suspensory (Cooper's) ligaments, which run from the dermis to the pectoral fascia, tethering and puckering the overlying skin (dimpling). Lactiferous duct involvement causes nipple retraction, and pectoral fascia involvement fixes the breast to the chest wall rather than dimpling the skin.",
