   "stem": "In a village of Assam, a man is observed walking with the help of a stick and has genu valgum. Many people in the same village present with similar symptoms. What is the most probable cause of this condition?",
   "options": [
    "Calcium deficiency",
    "Vitamin C deficiency",
    "Skeletal fluorosis",
    "Vitamin D deficiency (Osteomalacia)"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Genu valgum and skeletal deformity clustering in many villagers of a high-fluoride region (e.g. Assam) indicate endemic skeletal fluorosis from chronic fluoride in drinking water (osteosclerosis on X-ray, seen at 3-6 mg/L); it is prevented by defluoridation/safe water. Community clustering argues against isolated nutritional deficiency.",
   "reference": "FMGE July 2025 Part 2 (real exam recall); Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Environment and Health and Health Information",
