   "concept": "WHO recommends a rapid molecular test such as Xpert MTB/RIF (CBNAAT) as the initial diagnostic test for all forms of tuberculosis including spinal and other extrapulmonary disease, because it detects Mycobacterium tuberculosis and rifampicin resistance within about two hours on a biopsy or aspirate. Mycobacterial culture remains the microbiological gold standard and is still sent for full drug susceptibility, but it takes weeks and so cannot be the initial test. Radiographs and CT show the structural lesion but never confirm the organism.",
