   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Bempedoic acid is a dicarboxylic-acid prodrug activated to bempedoyl-CoA in liver, where it competitively inhibits ATP citrate lyase and so reduces cholesterol synthesis at a step upstream of HMG-CoA reductase. It is used with diet and statins for hypercholesterolaemia, and because activation requires a liver-specific enzyme it largely avoids the muscle toxicity of statins. Its inhibition of ATP citrate lyase is competitive, not non-competitive.",
