   "stem": "On day 5 of a febrile illness a teenager's fever settles but he develops severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, restlessness and cool peripheries. His haematocrit has risen 22% while the platelet count has fallen to 40,000/mm3. These 'warning signs' at defervescence most likely indicate:",
