   "topic": "Biostatistics: tests & distributions",
   "part": "B",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "In a large sample, serum cholesterol follows a symmetrical bell-shaped (normal) distribution. Approximately what proportion of observations lies within the mean plus or minus 2 standard deviations, and how do the mean, median and mode compare in this distribution?",
   "options": [
