   "stem": "A 26-year-old woman with 7 weeks of amenorrhoea and prior pelvic inflammatory disease presents with sudden severe left iliac fossa pain, one episode of syncope and right shoulder-tip pain. BP is 80/50 mmHg with tachycardia; there is cervical motion tenderness and fullness in the pouch of Douglas. Serum beta-hCG is 2600 and transvaginal scan shows an empty uterus with a left adnexal mass and free fluid. What is the most appropriate management?",
