   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A ventilated trauma patient becomes acutely hypotensive with a raised jugular venous pressure. A portable chest film shows a hyperlucent left hemithorax with absent lung markings, a deep left costophrenic sulcus, a depressed left hemidiaphragm and the trachea and mediastinum shifted to the right. What is the immediate management?",
