   "concept": "A hyperlucent hemithorax with absent lung markings plus contralateral mediastinal/tracheal shift and a depressed diaphragm indicates a tension pneumothorax, in which trapped air compresses the mediastinum and impairs venous return (shock, raised JVP). It is a clinical emergency treated by immediate needle decompression or chest drain - one must not wait for a CT. A haemothorax would appear opaque, not hyperlucent.",
