   "concept": "A full ('unfasted') stomach carries a high aspiration risk, so rapid sequence induction is used: pre-oxygenation, a swift IV induction agent plus a fast-acting muscle relaxant (classically suxamethonium), application of cricoid pressure and prompt intubation while avoiding routine positive-pressure mask ventilation that could inflate the stomach. Aspiration of gastric acid causes Mendelson's syndrome.",
