   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Pulseless electrical activity is a non-shockable rhythm: there is organised electrical activity without a pulse, so defibrillation is not indicated. Management is uninterrupted high-quality CPR with adrenaline and an active search for reversible causes (the 4 Hs and 4 Ts - hypoxia, hypovolaemia, hypo/hyperkalaemia, hypothermia; tension pneumothorax, tamponade, toxins, thrombosis). Only VF and pulseless VT are shocked.",
   "reference": "AHA Guidelines for CPR and ECC 2020, Ch. Adult Cardiac Arrest Algorithm; Morgan & Mikhail's Clinical Anesthesiology 6e, Ch. Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation",
