   "topic": "Coma, raised intracranial pressure & brain death",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Doll's eye movement (oculocephalic reflex) is absent when there is:",
   "options": [
    "Psychogenic unresponsiveness",
    "Brainstem dysfunction",
    "A hemispheric lesion only",
    "Cortical blindness"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The oculocephalic reflex requires intact vestibular nuclei, medial longitudinal fasciculus and third and sixth nerve nuclei, so its loss in a comatose patient indicates brainstem failure. It is testable only after excluding cervical spine injury.",
