    "Prothrombin time / INR",
    "Serum bilirubin"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Factor VII has the shortest half-life of the clotting factors, so the prothrombin time rises early and reflects synthetic function; albumin has a 20-day half-life and changes late, while transaminases indicate injury rather than function.",
