   "topic": "Poisoning & envenomation: emergency management",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The antidote for organophosphate poisoning is:",
   "options": [
    "Naloxone",
    "Flumazenil",
    "Methylene blue",
    "Atropine with pralidoxime"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Organophosphates irreversibly inhibit acetylcholinesterase, causing the muscarinic DUMBBELS features with miosis, bronchorrhoea and fasciculations. Atropine reverses muscarinic effects and pralidoxime reactivates the enzyme if given before ageing.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Cholinergic Drugs",
