   "topic": "Poisoning & envenomation: emergency management",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The characteristic feature of neurotoxic (cobra or krait) envenomation is:",
   "options": [
    "Bleeding from gums",
    "Local necrosis only",
    "Acute kidney injury",
    "Descending paralysis with ptosis and respiratory failure"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Elapid venom blocks the neuromuscular junction, producing ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, bulbar palsy and then respiratory paralysis with minimal local reaction, especially in krait bite which is often painless and nocturnal. Ventilation plus antivenom is life-saving.",
