   "topic": "Poisoning & envenomation: emergency management",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Methanol poisoning is treated with:",
   "options": [
    "Fomepizole or ethanol with sodium bicarbonate and haemodialysis",
    "Atropine",
    "N-acetylcysteine",
    "Naloxone"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Methanol is metabolised by alcohol dehydrogenase to formic acid, causing high anion gap acidosis and blindness. Fomepizole or ethanol competitively blocks the enzyme, and haemodialysis removes methanol and formate.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Ethyl and Methyl Alcohol",
