   "concept": "Charcoal does not bind metals such as iron and lithium, alcohols, strong acids and alkalis or cyanide, because these are small, highly ionised or poorly adsorbable molecules. Multi-dose charcoal is useful for carbamazepine, theophylline, dapsone and phenobarbitone.",
