    "Anaemia",
    "A single cardiac arrhythmia",
    "Epilepsy"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Falls in old age are almost always multifactorial, so assessment covers gait and balance, vision, cognition, postural blood pressure, footwear, home hazards and a full drug review. Falls are a leading cause of hip fracture and loss of independence.",
