   "topic": "Geriatrics, palliative care & end-of-life issues",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Delirium is distinguished from dementia principally by:",
   "options": [
    "Preserved attention",
    "Absence of any identifiable cause",
    "Progressive memory loss over years",
    "Acute onset with fluctuating course and impaired attention"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Delirium is an acute, fluctuating disturbance of attention and awareness with an underlying medical precipitant such as infection, drugs, retention or electrolyte disturbance, and is reversible; dementia is chronic and progressive with attention preserved until late.",
