   "topic": "Medical disorders in pregnancy: anaemia, diabetes, heart disease",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Anaemia in pregnancy as per WHO is defined as haemoglobin below:",
   "options": [
    "11 g/dL",
    "12 g/dL",
    "10 g/dL",
    "9 g/dL"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "WHO defines anaemia in pregnancy as haemoglobin below 11 g/dL; the Indian national programme grades 10 to 10.9 as mild, 7 to 9.9 as moderate, below 7 as severe and below 4 g/dL as very severe or decompensated.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Anaemia in Pregnancy",
