   "topic": "Infections in pregnancy & Rh isoimmunisation",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The most sensitive non-invasive test to detect fetal anaemia in Rh isoimmunisation is:",
   "options": [
    "Maternal haemoglobin",
    "Amniotic fluid index",
    "Middle cerebral artery peak systolic velocity on Doppler",
    "Biparietal diameter"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Anaemia lowers blood viscosity and raises cardiac output, increasing middle cerebral artery peak systolic velocity above 1.5 multiples of the median. It has replaced serial amniocentesis for bilirubin (Liley curve) in surveillance.",
   "reference": "Williams Obstetrics 26e, Ch. Alloimmunisation",
