   "topic": "Infections in pregnancy & Rh isoimmunisation",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The Kleihauer-Betke test is used to:",
   "options": [
    "Diagnose Rh incompatibility",
    "Detect maternal anaemia",
    "Measure fetal lung maturity",
    "Quantify fetomaternal haemorrhage to calculate the anti-D dose"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "The acid-elution Kleihauer test counts fetal cells resistant to acid in the maternal circulation, quantifying fetomaternal haemorrhage so additional anti-D can be given when the bleed exceeds 15 mL of fetal red cells.",
   "reference": "Williams Obstetrics 26e, Ch. Alloimmunisation",
