   "topic": "Infections in pregnancy & Rh isoimmunisation",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The classical triad of congenital rubella syndrome is:",
   "options": [
    "Hepatosplenomegaly, rash and jaundice",
    "Chorioretinitis, hydrocephalus and calcification",
    "Cataract, cardiac defect and deafness",
    "Limb defects, cleft palate and anaemia"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Congenital rubella causes cataract, patent ductus arteriosus or pulmonary artery stenosis and sensorineural deafness, with maximum risk in the first trimester. The intracranial calcification triad belongs to toxoplasmosis.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Rubella",
