    "Cytomegalovirus",
    "Rubella",
    "Toxoplasmosis",
    "Syphilis"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Congenital CMV affects about 0.5 to 1% of births, causing periventricular calcification, microcephaly, chorioretinitis, hepatosplenomegaly and blueberry-muffin rash, and is the leading infectious cause of sensorineural hearing loss.",
   "reference": "Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics 21e, Ch. Cytomegalovirus",
