   "topic": "Infections in pregnancy & Rh isoimmunisation",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "To prevent mother-to-child transmission of HIV, the current recommendation is:",
   "options": [
    "Lifelong maternal antiretroviral therapy with infant prophylaxis and exclusive feeding of one type",
    "Caesarean section for all",
    "Single-dose nevirapine to mother only",
    "Avoid all antiretrovirals in pregnancy"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Lifelong maternal ART reduces transmission to below 2%, with infant nevirapine prophylaxis and exclusive breastfeeding or exclusive replacement feeding, never mixed feeding. Vaginal delivery is acceptable when the viral load is suppressed.",
   "reference": "NACO National Guidelines for Prevention of Parent to Child Transmission of HIV 2017; Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. AIDS",
