   "topic": "Multiple pregnancy, polyhydramnios & IUGR",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Symmetrical intrauterine growth restriction most typically results from:",
   "options": [
    "Third trimester placental insufficiency",
    "Pre-eclampsia",
    "Post-term pregnancy",
    "An early insult such as infection or chromosomal anomaly"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Symmetrical growth restriction reflects an insult during the phase of cellular hyperplasia - infection, aneuploidy, drugs - reducing head and abdomen proportionately. Asymmetrical restriction with head sparing indicates late placental insufficiency.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. IUGR",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_OBG_MUL_005",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Obstetrics & Gynaecology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Multiple pregnancy, polyhydramnios & IUGR",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The most sensitive single ultrasound parameter for detecting growth restriction is:",
   "options": [
    "Head circumference",
    "Biparietal diameter",
    "Abdominal circumference",
    "Femur length"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Abdominal circumference reflects liver glycogen and subcutaneous fat and falls earliest in asymmetric restriction, so it is the most sensitive single biometric measure; serial measurement and Doppler guide timing of delivery.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. IUGR",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_OBG_MUL_006",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Obstetrics & Gynaecology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Multiple pregnancy, polyhydramnios & IUGR",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Oligohydramnios is defined as an amniotic fluid index below:",
   "options": [
    "5 cm",
    "15 cm",
    "2 cm",
    "10 cm"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "An amniotic fluid index below 5 cm or a single deepest pocket below 2 cm defines oligohydramnios, associated with renal agenesis, obstructive uropathy, ruptured membranes, growth restriction and post-term pregnancy.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. Oligohydramnios",
   "tags": [
