   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Multiple pregnancy, polyhydramnios & IUGR",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Vanishing twin syndrome refers to:",
   "options": [
    "Early loss and resorption of one twin diagnosed in the first trimester",
    "Twin reversed arterial perfusion",
    "Delivery of one twin only",
    "Death of both twins"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Spontaneous loss of one gestational sac in the first trimester with resorption of the tissue occurs in up to 20 to 30% of twin pregnancies detected early, usually with a good outcome for the survivor.",
   "reference": "Williams Obstetrics 26e, Ch. Multifetal Pregnancy",
   "tags": [
