   "topic": "Multiple pregnancy, polyhydramnios & IUGR",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The commonest complication of multiple pregnancy is:",
   "options": [
    "Preterm labour",
    "Oligohydramnios",
    "Post-term pregnancy",
    "Macrosomia"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Preterm labour is the commonest and most important complication of multiple pregnancy, with mean gestation at delivery of about 36 weeks for twins and 33 for triplets; anaemia, pre-eclampsia and postpartum haemorrhage are also increased.",
   "reference": "Williams Obstetrics 26e, Ch. Multifetal Pregnancy",
   "tags": [
