   "topic": "Preterm labour, PROM & post-term pregnancy",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Post-term pregnancy is defined as gestation beyond:",
   "options": [
    "42 completed weeks",
    "40 weeks",
    "41 weeks",
    "43 weeks"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Post-term means beyond 42 completed weeks, and carries risks of macrosomia, meconium aspiration, oligohydramnios, placental insufficiency and sudden intrauterine death, so induction is usually offered by 41 weeks.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. Post-maturity",
