   "topic": "Third-stage complications, retained placenta & uterine inversion",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The first step in managing a woman with brisk bleeding immediately after delivery is:",
   "options": [
    "Immediate laparotomy",
    "Immediate hysterectomy",
    "Await spontaneous cessation",
    "Uterine massage with an oxytocic while calling for help and securing intravenous access"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Simultaneous resuscitation and cause-directed treatment are needed: massage, oxytocics, bladder emptying, examination for tears and retained tissue, then bimanual compression, balloon tamponade and surgical measures if bleeding persists.",
