   "topic": "Infertility & assisted reproduction",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Infertility is defined as failure to conceive after:",
   "options": [
    "Three months",
    "Six months",
    "One year of regular unprotected intercourse",
    "Two years"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Twelve months of regular unprotected intercourse defines infertility, though evaluation begins earlier if the woman is over 35 or there is a known cause such as amenorrhoea, previous pelvic infection or undescended testes.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. Infertility",
   "tags": [
