   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Infertility & assisted reproduction",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The current first-line drug for ovulation induction in polycystic ovary syndrome is:",
   "options": [
    "Human menopausal gonadotropin",
    "Clomiphene citrate",
    "Bromocriptine",
    "Letrozole"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Letrozole, an aromatase inhibitor, gives higher live birth rates than clomiphene in polycystic ovary syndrome with fewer multiple pregnancies and no antioestrogenic effect on the endometrium.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Drugs for Infertility",
   "tags": [
