   "topic": "Endometriosis, adenomyosis & chronic pelvic pain",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The classical triad of symptoms in endometriosis is:",
   "options": [
    "Prolapse, incontinence and constipation",
    "Fever, discharge and bleeding",
    "Dysmenorrhoea, dyspareunia and infertility",
    "Amenorrhoea, obesity and hirsutism"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Endometriosis typically causes secondary dysmenorrhoea beginning before menses, deep dyspareunia, chronic pelvic pain and infertility. Symptom severity correlates poorly with the extent of disease.",
