   "topic": "Endometriosis, adenomyosis & chronic pelvic pain",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Adenomyosis characteristically presents with:",
   "options": [
    "Menorrhagia with dysmenorrhoea in a diffusely bulky tender uterus in a parous woman over 35",
    "Amenorrhoea in a nullipara",
    "Postmenopausal bleeding",
    "Acute pelvic pain in adolescence"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Adenomyosis is endometrial tissue within the myometrium, giving a symmetrically enlarged tender uterus with heavy painful periods, typically in multiparous women over 35. MRI or transvaginal ultrasound shows myometrial junctional zone thickening.",
