   "topic": "Endometriosis, adenomyosis & chronic pelvic pain",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Medical management of endometriosis works principally by:",
   "options": [
    "Stimulating ovulation",
    "Inducing a hypo-oestrogenic or progestogen-dominant state to cause atrophy of ectopic endometrium",
    "Antibiotic eradication",
    "Increasing oestrogen"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Continuous progestogens, combined oral contraceptives, GnRH analogues with add-back therapy and dienogest all suppress ovarian oestrogen or oppose it, causing decidualisation and atrophy of implants. They relieve pain but do not improve fertility.",
