   "topic": "Obstetric analgesia & anaesthesia; maternal mortality",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The preferred anaesthetic for an elective caesarean section is:",
   "options": [
    "Local infiltration",
    "Ketamine alone",
    "Spinal (subarachnoid) block",
    "General anaesthesia with intubation"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Regional anaesthesia avoids the risks of failed intubation and aspiration, keeps the mother awake and gives better neonatal outcomes, so spinal block is standard. General anaesthesia is reserved for extreme urgency or contraindications to regional block.",
