   "topic": "Obstetric analgesia & anaesthesia; maternal mortality",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Mendelson syndrome refers to:",
   "options": [
    "Amniotic fluid embolism",
    "Chemical aspiration pneumonitis from gastric contents during obstetric anaesthesia",
    "Postpartum pituitary necrosis",
    "Peripartum cardiomyopathy"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Aspiration of acidic gastric contents causes severe chemical pneumonitis with bronchospasm and hypoxia. Pregnant women are at high risk from a lax cardiac sphincter and delayed emptying, so fasting, antacids, H2 blockers and cricoid pressure are used.",
