   "topic": "Obstetric analgesia & anaesthesia; maternal mortality",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Supine hypotension syndrome in late pregnancy is caused by:",
   "options": [
    "Vagal overactivity",
    "Uterine contraction",
    "Compression of the inferior vena cava by the gravid uterus reducing venous return",
    "Spinal cord compression"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "In the supine position the gravid uterus compresses the inferior vena cava, reducing venous return, cardiac output and uterine perfusion, causing hypotension. Left lateral tilt relieves it and is routine during anaesthesia.",
