   "topic": "Prolapse, urogynaecology & genital fistula",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A ring pessary is most appropriate for prolapse in a woman who:",
   "options": [
    "Has cervical carcinoma",
    "Has a vesicovaginal fistula",
    "Wants definitive cure",
    "Is unfit for surgery, pregnant or wishes to defer operation"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "A pessary provides mechanical support as a temporising or palliative measure in women unfit for or declining surgery, in pregnancy or in the puerperium, but requires periodic change and local oestrogen to prevent ulceration.",
