   "topic": "Prolapse, urogynaecology & genital fistula",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The Fothergill (Manchester) operation for prolapse involves:",
   "options": [
    "Sacrocolpopexy",
    "Total hysterectomy",
    "Cervical amputation with plication of the cardinal ligaments and colporrhaphy",
    "Sling suspension"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "The Manchester operation amputates the elongated cervix and plicates the cardinal ligaments anterior to the cervical stump with anterior and posterior repair, conserving the uterus but often causing cervical stenosis and infertility.",
