   "topic": "Prolapse, urogynaecology & genital fistula",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Vault prolapse following hysterectomy is best treated by:",
   "options": [
    "Anterior colporrhaphy",
    "Repeat hysterectomy",
    "Pessary only",
    "Abdominal or laparoscopic sacrocolpopexy"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Sacrocolpopexy suspends the vault to the sacral promontory with mesh and has the best long-term durability; sacrospinous ligament fixation is the vaginal alternative. Prevention involves attaching the vault to the uterosacral ligaments at hysterectomy.",
