    "Three months of amenorrhoea",
    "Twelve consecutive months of amenorrhoea",
    "A single raised FSH",
    "Six months of amenorrhoea"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Menopause is the permanent cessation of menstruation confirmed after 12 months of amenorrhoea, occurring at a mean age of about 46 to 47 years in Indian women. Premature menopause is cessation before 40 years.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. Menopause",
