   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Menopause, HRT & osteoporosis",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The hormonal profile of the postmenopausal woman shows:",
   "options": [
    "High FSH and LH with low oestradiol",
    "Low FSH and low LH",
    "High oestradiol and high progesterone",
    "Low FSH with high oestradiol"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Loss of ovarian follicles removes negative feedback, so FSH rises markedly - more than LH because inhibin B also falls - while oestradiol falls. An FSH above 40 IU/L supports the diagnosis.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. Menopause",
