   "topic": "Menopause, HRT & osteoporosis",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The first-line pharmacological treatment of postmenopausal osteoporosis is:",
   "options": [
    "Oestrogen alone in all women",
    "A bisphosphonate with calcium and vitamin D",
    "Calcitonin",
    "Fluoride"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Bisphosphonates such as alendronate or zoledronate inhibit osteoclastic resorption and reduce vertebral and hip fracture risk, given with adequate calcium and vitamin D. Oral bisphosphonates must be taken upright and fasting to avoid oesophagitis.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Drugs for Osteoporosis",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
