   "topic": "Gestational trophoblastic disease & vulvo-vaginal lesions",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The classical ultrasound appearance of a complete hydatidiform mole is:",
   "options": [
    "An empty uterus",
    "A snowstorm appearance with no fetal parts and often bilateral theca lutein cysts",
    "A single gestational sac with a live fetus",
    "A thickened endometrium only"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The snowstorm or cluster-of-grapes pattern reflects hydropic villi, with a uterus large for dates, very high hCG and theca lutein cysts from hCG hyperstimulation. Hyperemesis, early pre-eclampsia and hyperthyroidism may occur.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. GTD",
