   "topic": "Newborn assessment, prematurity & low birth weight",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The first step in neonatal resuscitation of an apnoeic term baby is:",
   "options": [
    "Drying, warmth, positioning and clearing the airway, then positive pressure ventilation",
    "Chest compressions",
    "Intravenous adrenaline",
    "Sodium bicarbonate"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Initial steps are warmth, drying, stimulation and airway positioning; if the baby remains apnoeic or the heart rate is below 100, positive pressure ventilation is begun within the golden minute. Ventilation, not compression, is the priority in newborns because the cause is usually respiratory.",
   "reference": "Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics 21e, Ch. Neonatal Resuscitation",
