   "topic": "Newborn assessment, prematurity & low birth weight",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Chest compressions in neonatal resuscitation are started when the heart rate remains below:",
   "options": [
    "60 beats per minute despite 30 seconds of effective ventilation",
    "100 beats per minute",
    "80 beats per minute",
    "40 beats per minute"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Compressions begin at a heart rate below 60 after adequate ventilation, at a compression to ventilation ratio of 3 to 1. Adrenaline is given if the rate remains below 60 despite coordinated compressions and ventilation.",
