   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Newborn assessment, prematurity & low birth weight",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Delayed cord clamping in a term newborn is recommended because it:",
   "options": [
    "Prevents jaundice",
    "Reduces birth weight",
    "Improves iron stores and reduces anaemia in infancy",
    "Prevents infection"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Clamping after 1 to 3 minutes allows placental transfusion of about 80 mL of blood, improving haemoglobin and iron stores for up to six months, at the cost of a small increase in phototherapy requirement.",
   "reference": "WHO Guideline on Delayed Umbilical Cord Clamping 2014; Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics 21e, Ch. Delivery Room Care",
