    "Shigella",
    "Entamoeba histolytica",
    "Giardia",
    "Rotavirus"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Rotavirus is the leading cause of severe dehydrating diarrhoea in infants, now preventable by rotavirus vaccine included in the Indian universal immunisation programme. Shigella typically causes dysentery with blood and mucus.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Diarrhoeal Diseases",
