   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Zinc supplementation in childhood diarrhoea is recommended because it:",
   "options": [
    "Stops vomiting",
    "Treats the infection",
    "Replaces ORS",
    "Reduces the duration and severity of the episode and recurrence over the following months"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Zinc 20 mg daily for 14 days, or 10 mg under six months, shortens the episode by about 25% and reduces stool volume and recurrence, by restoring mucosal integrity and immune function.",
