   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Antibiotics in acute childhood diarrhoea are indicated for:",
   "options": [
    "Rotavirus diarrhoea",
    "All watery diarrhoea",
    "Any diarrhoea over 3 days",
    "Bloody diarrhoea (dysentery), suspected cholera and severe malnutrition with diarrhoea"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Most acute watery diarrhoea is viral and self-limiting; antibiotics are given for dysentery, suspected cholera with severe dehydration, and diarrhoea in severe acute malnutrition. Antimotility agents are contraindicated in children.",
