   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The commonest electrolyte abnormality complicating severe childhood diarrhoea is:",
   "options": [
    "Hypercalcaemia",
    "Hyperkalaemia with alkalosis",
    "Hypermagnesaemia",
    "Hypokalaemia with metabolic acidosis"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Stool losses of potassium and bicarbonate produce hypokalaemia with normal anion gap metabolic acidosis, causing abdominal distension, ileus and weakness. Potassium is added once urine output is established.",
