   "topic": "Acute respiratory infection, pneumonia & bronchiolitis",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "In IMNCI, fast breathing in a child aged 12 months to 5 years is defined as a respiratory rate of:",
   "options": [
    "30 or more",
    "50 or more",
    "40 breaths per minute or more",
    "60 or more"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Age-specific cut-offs are 60 or more below 2 months, 50 or more from 2 to 12 months and 40 or more from 12 months to 5 years. Fast breathing with cough indicates pneumonia in the IMNCI algorithm.",
