   "topic": "Acute respiratory infection, pneumonia & bronchiolitis",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Under the Government of India IMNCI classification, chest indrawing with cough in a 2-year-old child classifies the illness as:",
   "options": [
    "Bronchial asthma",
    "Severe pneumonia requiring referral and injectable antibiotics",
    "No pneumonia",
    "Pneumonia treated at home"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Lower chest indrawing indicates severe pneumonia; danger signs such as inability to drink, persistent vomiting, convulsions, lethargy or stridor at rest mandate urgent referral with a first dose of injectable antibiotic and oxygen.",
   "reference": "Government of India IMNCI Physicians Chart Booklet 2019; OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Respiratory System",
