    "Delivered by elective caesarean",
    "Small for gestational age at 28 weeks",
    "Extremely preterm"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Post-term or growth-restricted fetuses pass meconium with hypoxic stress and gasp it into the airways, causing patchy infiltrates, hyperinflation and pneumothorax risk with persistent pulmonary hypertension. Routine intrapartum suctioning is no longer advised.",
