    "Klinefelter syndrome",
    "Turner syndrome",
    "Down syndrome (trisomy 21)"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Trisomy 21 is the commonest chromosomal disorder compatible with survival and the leading chromosomal cause of intellectual disability, incidence rising with maternal age. Ninety-five percent result from meiotic non-disjunction.",
