   "stem": "A Down syndrome child is at greatest risk of which cardiac lesion?",
   "options": [
    "Endocardial cushion (atrioventricular septal) defect",
    "Coarctation of aorta",
    "Bicuspid aortic valve",
    "Tetralogy of Fallot"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Atrioventricular septal defect is the characteristic lesion in trisomy 21, occurring in about 40% with congenital heart disease. Duodenal atresia, atlantoaxial instability, hypothyroidism and leukaemia are other associations.",
