    "Robertsonian translocation Down syndrome"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "About 4% of Down syndrome is due to a Robertsonian translocation, usually 14;21; when inherited from a balanced carrier parent the recurrence risk is high, which is why karyotyping of the child and parents guides counselling.",
