   "topic": "Inborn errors, newborn screening & chromosomal syndromes",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Congenital hypothyroidism is screened for in the newborn because:",
   "options": [
    "It resolves spontaneously",
    "Untreated it causes irreversible intellectual disability and clinical signs are absent at birth",
    "It is always symptomatic",
    "It only affects growth"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Newborns are clinically normal because maternal thyroxine crosses the placenta, yet delay in starting thyroxine causes permanent intellectual disability - so screening at 48 to 72 hours by TSH is universally recommended.",
