   "topic": "Inborn errors, newborn screening & chromosomal syndromes",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The commonest inherited cause of intellectual disability, associated with macro-orchidism and a long face, is:",
   "options": [
    "Fragile X syndrome",
    "Down syndrome",
    "Angelman syndrome",
    "Prader-Willi syndrome"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Fragile X results from CGG trinucleotide repeat expansion in FMR1 with X-linked dominant inheritance and anticipation, causing intellectual disability, large ears, long face, macro-orchidism and autistic features. It is the commonest inherited (not chromosomal) cause.",
   "reference": "Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics 21e, Ch. Fragile X",
   "tags": [
