   "topic": "Childhood tuberculosis & paediatric HIV",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A Mantoux test is read as positive in a child when the induration is:",
   "options": [
    "20 mm or more",
    "Any induration",
    "5 mm of erythema",
    "10 mm or more at 48 to 72 hours"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Induration of 10 mm or more measured transversely at 48 to 72 hours is positive in India; 5 mm is used in severely immunocompromised or malnourished children. Erythema is not measured, and the test indicates infection, not active disease.",
   "reference": "National Tuberculosis Elimination Programme Guidelines for Paediatric Tuberculosis 2022; OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Tuberculosis",
