   "topic": "Childhood tuberculosis & paediatric HIV",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The commonest form of extrapulmonary tuberculosis in children is:",
   "options": [
    "Tuberculous meningitis",
    "Tuberculous lymphadenitis",
    "Spinal tuberculosis",
    "Abdominal tuberculosis"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Peripheral lymph node tuberculosis, usually cervical, is the commonest extrapulmonary form, presenting as matted painless nodes that may form a cold abscess and sinus. Tuberculous meningitis is the most lethal form.",
   "reference": "OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Tuberculosis",
   "tags": [
