   "topic": "Childhood tuberculosis & paediatric HIV",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "BCG vaccine is given at birth and protects best against:",
   "options": [
    "Disseminated tuberculosis and tuberculous meningitis in children",
    "Reinfection in adults",
    "Adult pulmonary tuberculosis",
    "Leprosy only"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "BCG gives about 60 to 80% protection against severe disseminated disease and tuberculous meningitis in young children but poor and variable protection against adult pulmonary tuberculosis. It is a live attenuated vaccine given intradermally.",
