    "Haematuria"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Nephrotic syndrome is heavy proteinuria, hypoalbuminaemia below 2.5 g/dL, oedema and hyperlipidaemia. Significant haematuria, hypertension or renal failure are atypical features suggesting a lesion other than minimal change disease.",
