   "topic": "Paediatric nephrology: nephrotic syndrome, UTI, AGN",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Steroid-resistant nephrotic syndrome is defined as failure of remission after:",
   "options": [
    "Four to six weeks of daily adequate prednisolone",
    "Three months of alternate-day therapy",
    "One week",
    "Two doses"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Failure to achieve remission after four to six weeks of daily prednisolone at 2 mg/kg defines steroid resistance and warrants renal biopsy, which usually shows focal segmental glomerulosclerosis rather than minimal change disease.",
