    "One to three weeks",
    "Six months"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Nephritis follows pharyngitis by 1 to 2 weeks and skin infection by 3 to 6 weeks, presenting with smoky urine, periorbital oedema, hypertension and oliguria, with low C3 and raised ASO or anti-DNase B titres.",
