    "Age under 1 year",
    "Age 1 to 10 years with a white cell count below 50,000 and hyperdiploidy"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Good prognostic factors are age 1 to 10, presenting white cell count under 50,000, B-cell precursor lineage, hyperdiploidy or ETV6-RUNX1 fusion, and rapid clearance of minimal residual disease. Infancy, hyperleucocytosis and BCR-ABL are adverse.",
