   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Vitamin K deficiency bleeding of the newborn is prevented by:",
   "options": [
    "Vitamin D drops",
    "Intramuscular vitamin K 1 mg at birth",
    "Oral iron",
    "Breastfeeding alone"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Newborns have low stores and sterile gut, and breast milk is low in vitamin K, so a single intramuscular dose at birth prevents classical and late haemorrhagic disease, the latter often presenting as intracranial bleeding at 2 to 12 weeks.",
