   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Physiological anaemia of infancy reaches its nadir at about:",
   "options": [
    "8 to 12 weeks of age",
    "1 week",
    "6 months",
    "1 year"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "After birth, rising oxygen saturation suppresses erythropoietin and fetal red cells have a shorter lifespan, so haemoglobin falls to about 10 to 11 g/dL by 8 to 12 weeks in term infants before recovering. No treatment is needed.",
