   "topic": "Anatomy & physiology of the ear; audiological tests",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "In Rinne's test, a negative result (bone conduction better than air conduction) indicates:",
   "options": [
    "Normal hearing",
    "Conductive hearing loss in the tested ear",
    "Sensorineural hearing loss",
    "Malingering"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "A negative Rinne means bone conduction exceeds air conduction, indicating conductive loss of at least 15 to 20 dB in that ear. In sensorineural loss, Rinne stays positive because both conductions fall together.",
   "reference": "Dhingra Diseases of Ear, Nose and Throat 8e, Ch. Assessment of Hearing",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
