   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Anatomy & physiology of the ear; audiological tests",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "In Weber's test, lateralisation of the sound to the affected ear suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Normal hearing",
    "Otosclerosis of the opposite ear",
    "Sensorineural loss in that ear",
    "Conductive hearing loss in that ear"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Sound lateralises to the ear with conductive loss because masking ambient noise is reduced and bone conduction is enhanced, whereas in sensorineural loss it lateralises to the better hearing ear.",
   "reference": "Dhingra Diseases of Ear, Nose and Throat 8e, Ch. Assessment of Hearing",
   "tags": [
