   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Anatomy & physiology of the ear; audiological tests",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The ossicular chain amplifies sound principally by:",
   "options": [
    "Resonance of the external canal alone",
    "The areal ratio of tympanic membrane to stapes footplate and the lever action of the ossicles",
    "Fluid movement in the semicircular canals",
    "Contraction of the stapedius"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Impedance matching between air and cochlear fluid is achieved by a 17 to 1 areal ratio and a 1.3 to 1 ossicular lever, giving about 22 to 25 dB of gain. Loss of this mechanism produces conductive deafness.",
   "reference": "Ganong's Review of Medical Physiology 26e, Ch. Hearing",
