   "topic": "Anatomy & physiology of the ear; audiological tests",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Pure tone audiometry showing an air-bone gap indicates:",
   "options": [
    "Normal hearing",
    "Retrocochlear pathology",
    "Conductive component of hearing loss",
    "Pure sensorineural loss"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "The air-bone gap quantifies the conductive component; a mixed loss shows both a raised bone conduction threshold and an air-bone gap. Speech audiometry and brainstem responses assess retrocochlear lesions.",
