   "topic": "Behavioural & developmental disorders; adolescent health",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Sydenham chorea following streptococcal infection is a major criterion of:",
   "options": [
    "Acute rheumatic fever",
    "Huntington disease",
    "Cerebral palsy",
    "Wilson disease"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Sydenham chorea is a major Jones criterion, appearing months after streptococcal infection with choreiform movements, emotional lability and hypotonia, and is self-limiting but requires secondary penicillin prophylaxis.",
   "reference": "Nelson Textbook of Pediatrics 21e, Ch. Rheumatic Fever",
