   "topic": "Behavioural & developmental disorders; adolescent health",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Specific learning disability such as dyslexia is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Difficulty in reading despite normal intelligence and adequate schooling",
    "Global intellectual disability",
    "Poor school attendance alone",
    "Hearing impairment"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Specific learning disability is unexpected underachievement in reading, writing or arithmetic despite normal intelligence, adequate instruction and intact senses, requiring formal psychoeducational assessment and remedial education with examination accommodations.",
   "reference": "OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Learning Disability",
   "tags": [
