   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Pediatrics",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "PEM, breastfeeding, micronutrients",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "In severe acute malnutrition, the rehydration fluid of choice for a dehydrated child is:",
   "options": [
    "Standard WHO ORS",
    "Normal saline boluses",
    "ReSoMal, which has lower sodium and higher potassium than standard ORS",
    "Plain water"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Malnourished children have excess total body sodium and depleted potassium, so ReSoMal with reduced sodium, added potassium and magnesium is used orally, given slowly because of the risk of fluid overload and heart failure.",
   "reference": "WHO Guideline: Updates on the Management of Severe Acute Malnutrition in Infants and Children 2013; OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Nutrition and Malnutrition",
   "tags": [
