    "Progressive bilateral conductive deafness with a normal tympanic membrane and paracusis willisii",
    "Acute otalgia"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Fixation of the stapes footplate by otosclerotic bone gives painless progressive conductive loss, often worsening in pregnancy, with a normal drum, absent stapedial reflex, Carhart's notch and paradoxically better hearing in noise (paracusis willisii).",
