   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "External & middle ear disease: otitis externa, otosclerosis",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The definitive treatment of otosclerosis with significant conductive loss is:",
   "options": [
    "Stapedotomy or stapedectomy with prosthesis",
    "Tympanoplasty",
    "Myringotomy",
    "Mastoidectomy"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Stapedotomy with a piston prosthesis restores ossicular continuity with excellent results; a hearing aid is an alternative for those unfit or unwilling. Surgery is avoided in an only-hearing ear.",
