   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "External & middle ear disease: otitis externa, otosclerosis",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A retracted tympanic membrane with conductive deafness and a type C tympanogram in a child suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Cholesteatoma",
    "Acute suppurative otitis media",
    "Otitis media with effusion from eustachian tube dysfunction",
    "Otosclerosis"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Eustachian dysfunction, commonly from adenoid hypertrophy or allergy, causes negative middle ear pressure, retraction and serous effusion with painless hearing loss. Persistent cases need grommet insertion with adenoidectomy.",
