   "topic": "External & middle ear disease: otitis externa, otosclerosis",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The tubotympanic (safe) type of chronic suppurative otitis media is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "A central perforation with mucoid non-offensive discharge",
    "A marginal perforation with foul discharge",
    "Facial palsy",
    "Granulation and polyp"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Safe disease shows a central perforation of the pars tensa with intermittent mucoid non-foul discharge and no bone erosion, managed by aural toilet, topical antibiotics and later tympanoplasty.",
   "reference": "Dhingra Diseases of Ear, Nose and Throat 8e, Ch. CSOM",
