   "topic": "External & middle ear disease: otitis externa, otosclerosis",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Cholesteatoma is best described as:",
   "options": [
    "A malignant neoplasm",
    "A collection of serous fluid",
    "Keratinising stratified squamous epithelium in the middle ear that erodes bone",
    "A benign tumour of cholesterol"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Despite its name, cholesteatoma contains no cholesterol and is not a tumour: it is trapped keratinising squamous epithelium producing progressive bone destruction, so the only definitive treatment is surgical removal.",
