   "topic": "External & middle ear disease: otitis externa, otosclerosis",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Traumatic perforation of the tympanic membrane is usually managed by:",
   "options": [
    "Keeping the ear dry and observing, as most heal spontaneously",
    "Immediate tympanoplasty",
    "Syringing the ear",
    "Topical ototoxic drops"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Most traumatic perforations heal within weeks with dry ear precautions and avoidance of syringing and ototoxic drops. Surgery is considered only if the perforation persists beyond three months or hearing loss suggests ossicular injury.",
