   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Vertigo, Meniere's disease & facial nerve palsy",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The classical triad of Meniere disease is:",
   "options": [
    "Episodic vertigo, fluctuating sensorineural hearing loss and tinnitus with aural fullness",
    "Headache, vomiting and diplopia",
    "Conductive deafness, tinnitus and otalgia",
    "Vertigo, facial palsy and otorrhoea"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Meniere disease results from endolymphatic hydrops, giving episodic vertigo lasting 20 minutes to several hours, low-frequency fluctuating sensorineural loss, tinnitus and aural fullness. Salt restriction, betahistine and diuretics are used.",
   "reference": "Dhingra Diseases of Ear, Nose and Throat 8e, Ch. Meniere's Disease",
   "tags": [
