   "topic": "Vertigo, Meniere's disease & facial nerve palsy",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Bell palsy is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Sparing of the forehead",
    "Lower motor neuron facial palsy with inability to wrinkle the forehead on the affected side",
    "Bilateral ptosis",
    "Isolated lower lip weakness"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "A lower motor neuron lesion affects the whole hemiface including the frontalis, unlike an upper motor neuron lesion where bilateral cortical innervation spares the forehead. Bell palsy is idiopathic, possibly HSV-related, treated with early corticosteroids.",
   "reference": "Dhingra Diseases of Ear, Nose and Throat 8e, Ch. Facial Nerve",
   "tags": [
