    "Meniere disease",
    "Otosclerosis",
    "Vestibular schwannoma (acoustic neuroma) at the cerebellopontine angle"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "A vestibular schwannoma causes asymmetrical sensorineural loss with poor speech discrimination and tinnitus, then trigeminal involvement with a diminished corneal reflex, and later facial and cerebellar signs. Gadolinium MRI is the investigation of choice.",
