   "stem": "Healing of a clean surgical incision with apposed edges is termed:",
   "options": [
    "Hypertrophic healing",
    "Healing by primary intention",
    "Healing by secondary intention",
    "Healing by tertiary intention"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Primary intention healing occurs when edges are approximated with minimal tissue loss, giving a fine scar. Secondary intention involves granulation and contraction across a gaping wound, and tertiary (delayed primary) closure follows a period of open management.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Wound Healing",
