    "Occurs only in the elderly"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Keloids grow beyond the original wound boundary, recur after excision and are commoner in darker skin and over the sternum, shoulder and earlobe. Hypertrophic scars stay within the wound and often regress, especially across flexures after burns.",
