   "topic": "Head injury & neurosurgical emergencies",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Diffuse axonal injury is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "A lucid interval",
    "A large focal haematoma",
    "Rapid full recovery",
    "Immediate prolonged coma with relatively normal initial CT and petechial haemorrhages at grey-white junctions"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Rotational acceleration-deceleration shears axons, causing immediate and prolonged unconsciousness with a CT that may look near-normal; MRI shows lesions at the grey-white junction, corpus callosum and brainstem. Prognosis is poor.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Head Injury",
   "tags": [
