   "stem": "A split-thickness skin graft consists of:",
   "options": [
    "Dermis with subcutaneous fat",
    "Epidermis only",
    "Epidermis with part of the dermis",
    "Epidermis and full dermis"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Split-thickness grafts include epidermis and a variable part of dermis, take more readily on imperfect beds and allow donor site re-epithelialisation, but contract more. Full-thickness grafts contract less and give better cosmesis but need an excellent bed.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Plastic Surgery",
