   "topic": "Burns & basics of plastic surgery",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The commonest cause of death in the first 24 to 48 hours after a major burn is:",
   "options": [
    "Sepsis",
    "Curling ulcer",
    "Renal failure",
    "Hypovolaemic shock from capillary leak"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Massive capillary leak causes burn shock and death early if resuscitation is inadequate; beyond the first week, sepsis and multi-organ failure become the leading causes. Curling ulcer is a stress ulcer complication.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Burns",
   "tags": [
