   "topic": "Oesophagus, stomach & gastric carcinoma",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Progressive dysphagia to solids then liquids in an elderly smoker suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Achalasia cardia",
    "Plummer-Vinson syndrome",
    "Carcinoma of the oesophagus",
    "Diffuse oesophageal spasm"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Mechanical obstruction causes dysphagia first to solids progressing to liquids with weight loss, whereas motility disorders such as achalasia cause dysphagia to both from the outset. Endoscopy with biopsy is the investigation of choice.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Oesophagus",
   "tags": [
