   "topic": "Oesophagus, stomach & gastric carcinoma",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Achalasia cardia is characterised manometrically by:",
   "options": [
    "Failure of relaxation of the lower oesophageal sphincter with absent peristalsis",
    "Normal peristalsis",
    "Hypotensive lower oesophageal sphincter",
    "Uncoordinated high-amplitude contractions only"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Loss of inhibitory myenteric neurons produces a non-relaxing hypertensive sphincter with aperistalsis, giving a bird-beak appearance on barium swallow. Pneumatic dilatation, Heller myotomy or POEM are treatment options.",
