   "topic": "Fluid, electrolyte & nutritional support in surgery",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Syndrome of inappropriate ADH secretion after surgery produces:",
   "options": [
    "Euvolaemic hyponatraemia with concentrated urine and high urinary sodium",
    "Hypovolaemic hypernatraemia",
    "Dilute urine",
    "Low urinary sodium"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "SIADH gives hyponatraemia with inappropriately concentrated urine, urinary sodium above 40 mmol/L and clinical euvolaemia, with low serum osmolality. Fluid restriction is first-line; correction must be gradual.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Fluid and Electrolytes",
   "tags": [
