  {
   "id": "Q_SUR_LIV_006",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Surgery",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Liver, spleen & portal hypertension surgery",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "In hydatid cyst of the liver, the danger of percutaneous aspiration is:",
   "options": [
    "Bile leak only",
    "Infection only",
    "Anaphylaxis and dissemination of daughter cysts",
    "Bleeding only"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Spillage of cyst contents can cause anaphylactic shock and peritoneal seeding. If PAIR is performed it is done under albendazole cover with a scolicidal agent; surgery involves careful removal without spillage.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Liver",
   "tags": [
