   "topic": "Liver, spleen & portal hypertension surgery",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The most feared long-term complication after splenectomy is:",
   "options": [
    "Renal failure",
    "Pulmonary fibrosis",
    "Overwhelming post-splenectomy infection by encapsulated organisms",
    "Portal hypertension"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Loss of splenic macrophages and opsonisation predisposes to fulminant sepsis from pneumococcus, meningococcus and Haemophilus influenzae. Vaccination at least two weeks before elective splenectomy and prophylactic penicillin are essential.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Spleen",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
