   "topic": "Liver, spleen & portal hypertension surgery",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Alpha-fetoprotein is most useful as a tumour marker in:",
   "options": [
    "Colorectal carcinoma",
    "Gastric carcinoma",
    "Pancreatic carcinoma",
    "Hepatocellular carcinoma and non-seminomatous germ cell tumours"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "AFP is raised in hepatocellular carcinoma, used with ultrasound for surveillance in cirrhosis, and in yolk sac and embryonal elements of testicular tumours. Pure seminoma does not raise AFP.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Liver",
   "tags": [
