   "topic": "Liver, spleen & portal hypertension surgery",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Budd-Chiari syndrome is caused by:",
   "options": [
    "Splenic vein thrombosis",
    "Hepatic venous outflow obstruction, presenting with hepatomegaly, ascites and abdominal pain",
    "Biliary obstruction",
    "Portal vein thrombosis"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Occlusion of the hepatic veins or suprahepatic inferior vena cava, often from a myeloproliferative disorder or thrombophilia, causes tender hepatomegaly with intractable ascites and caudate lobe hypertrophy from its separate venous drainage.",
   "reference": "Bailey & Love's Short Practice of Surgery 28e, Ch. Liver",
   "tags": [
