   "topic": "Haemodynamics: oedema, thrombosis, embolism, infarction, shock",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Virchow triad describing the pathogenesis of thrombosis comprises:",
   "options": [
    "Infection, inflammation and ischaemia",
    "Hypoxia, acidosis and hypercapnia",
    "Anaemia, leucocytosis and thrombocytosis",
    "Endothelial injury, abnormal blood flow and hypercoagulability"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Endothelial injury is dominant in arterial and cardiac thrombosis, while stasis or turbulence and hypercoagulable states dominate in venous thrombosis. The triad guides both prophylaxis and treatment.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. Haemodynamic Disorders",
   "tags": [
