   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Haemodynamics: oedema, thrombosis, embolism, infarction, shock",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Fat embolism syndrome classically follows:",
   "options": [
    "Deep vein thrombosis",
    "Long bone fractures, presenting with dyspnoea, petechiae and confusion 24 to 72 hours later",
    "Central line insertion",
    "Caesarean section"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Marrow fat enters torn venules after long bone or pelvic fracture, producing the triad of respiratory distress, neurological change and a petechial rash over the upper trunk and conjunctiva after a latent interval.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. Haemodynamic Disorders",
   "tags": [
