   "topic": "Haemodynamics: oedema, thrombosis, embolism, infarction, shock",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Transudative oedema differs from exudate in having:",
   "options": [
    "High LDH",
    "Many inflammatory cells",
    "Low protein content with specific gravity below 1.012",
    "High protein and high specific gravity"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Transudates result from altered Starling forces - raised hydrostatic or reduced oncotic pressure - and are protein-poor, whereas exudates follow increased vascular permeability in inflammation and are protein and cell rich.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. Haemodynamic Disorders",
