   "topic": "Haemodynamics: oedema, thrombosis, embolism, infarction, shock",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Which type of shock is characterised by warm peripheries with low systemic vascular resistance?",
   "options": [
    "Hypovolaemic shock",
    "Septic (distributive) shock",
    "Obstructive shock",
    "Cardiogenic shock"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Distributive shock from sepsis or anaphylaxis causes vasodilatation with a high cardiac output and warm peripheries in the early phase, unlike hypovolaemic and cardiogenic shock which show cold, clammy, vasoconstricted skin.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. Shock",
   "tags": [
