   "stem": "The commonest source of a systemic arterial embolus is:",
   "options": [
    "Pulmonary veins",
    "Deep veins of the leg",
    "Mural thrombus in the left heart",
    "Portal vein"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "About 80% of systemic emboli arise from intracardiac mural thrombi complicating myocardial infarction, atrial fibrillation or valve disease, lodging most often in the lower limbs, brain, gut, kidney and spleen.",
