   "stem": "The commonest histological type of invasive breast carcinoma is:",
   "options": [
    "Medullary carcinoma",
    "Mucinous carcinoma",
    "Invasive ductal carcinoma of no special type",
    "Invasive lobular carcinoma"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Invasive ductal carcinoma, now called invasive carcinoma of no special type, accounts for about 70 to 80%, forming a hard scirrhous mass with desmoplasia. Lobular carcinoma is often bilateral and multicentric with single-file infiltration from E-cadherin loss.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. The Breast",
