    "Is premalignant",
    "Causes nipple discharge",
    "Always resolves within a day"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Fat necrosis produces a hard irregular mass with skin tethering and calcification that closely mimics malignancy, usually after trauma or surgery. Histology shows lipid-laden macrophages, and biopsy is needed to exclude cancer.",
