   "topic": "Endocrine pathology: thyroid, adrenal, pituitary, MEN",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Fine needle aspiration cytology cannot distinguish follicular adenoma from follicular carcinoma because:",
   "options": [
    "Cytology is always inadequate",
    "Malignancy is defined by capsular or vascular invasion, which requires histology of the whole capsule",
    "There are no follicular cells",
    "Cells look malignant in both"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Both lesions have identical cytological appearances, so the distinction requires demonstration of capsular or vascular invasion in an excised specimen - hence a report of follicular neoplasm mandates diagnostic lobectomy.",
