    "Crohn disease",
    "Foreign body reaction",
    "Sarcoidosis",
    "Tuberculosis"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Central caseous necrosis with a cheesy appearance is typical of tuberculosis, resulting from combined hypersensitivity and mycobacterial lipids. Sarcoidosis, Crohn disease and berylliosis produce non-caseating granulomas.",
