   "stem": "The Ghon complex in primary pulmonary tuberculosis consists of:",
   "options": [
    "Miliary nodules",
    "A subpleural parenchymal focus with draining hilar lymph node involvement",
    "Pleural effusion alone",
    "An apical cavity"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The Ghon focus lies in the lower part of the upper lobe or upper part of the lower lobe; with its draining hilar node it forms the Ghon (primary) complex, which usually heals by fibrosis and calcification (Ranke complex).",
