   "topic": "Immunodeficiency, transplant rejection & HLA",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Acute cellular rejection of a renal allograft is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Interstitial mononuclear infiltrate with tubulitis, responsive to increased immunosuppression",
    "Interstitial fibrosis and tubular atrophy",
    "Granuloma formation",
    "Vascular thrombosis within minutes"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "T-cell mediated rejection occurring days to months after transplantation shows lymphocytic infiltration with tubulitis and endarteritis, and generally responds to pulse corticosteroids or anti-lymphocyte therapy.",
