   "topic": "Immunodeficiency, transplant rejection & HLA",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Graft-versus-host disease characteristically affects:",
   "options": [
    "Skin, gut and liver, after allogeneic bone marrow transplantation",
    "Kidney and heart",
    "Brain",
    "Lung only"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Immunocompetent donor T cells attack recipient tissues, producing rash, diarrhoea and cholestatic jaundice. Prevention uses HLA matching and immunosuppression; irradiation of blood products prevents transfusion-associated GVHD.",
   "reference": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease 10e, Ch. Diseases of the Immune System",
