   "topic": "Immunodeficiency, transplant rejection & HLA",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "X-linked agammaglobulinaemia (Bruton disease) is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Absent neutrophils",
    "Absent T cells",
    "Absent B cells and immunoglobulins with recurrent pyogenic infections after six months of age",
    "Complement deficiency"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "BTK gene mutation blocks B-cell maturation, so infections with encapsulated bacteria begin as maternal IgG wanes at about 6 months. Tonsils and lymph nodes are absent; treatment is immunoglobulin replacement.",
