   "topic": "Concepts of health & disease, natural history, levels of prevention",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The WHO definition of health is:",
   "options": [
    "Absence of disease",
    "A state of complete physical, mental and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity",
    "Physical fitness",
    "Long life expectancy"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The 1948 WHO definition is criticised as idealistic and unmeasurable, but remains foundational; a spiritual dimension and the concept of quality of life have since been added in operational definitions.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Concept of Health and Disease",
