   "topic": "Concepts of health & disease, natural history, levels of prevention",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "One DALY is best defined as:",
   "options": [
    "One death",
    "One lost year of healthy life, combining years of life lost and years lived with disability",
    "One hospital admission",
    "One year of illness"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The disability-adjusted life year combines premature mortality (YLL) and morbidity (YLD) into a single measure of disease burden, allowing comparison across conditions and guiding priority setting.",
