   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The vector of lymphatic filariasis in India is:",
   "options": [
    "Culex quinquefasciatus, breeding in dirty polluted water",
    "Anopheles stephensi",
    "Phlebotomus",
    "Aedes aegypti"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Culex quinquefasciatus, a night biter breeding in organically polluted water, transmits Wuchereria bancrofti which causes over 95% of Indian filariasis. Mass drug administration with DEC and albendazole is the control strategy.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Filariasis",
