   "topic": "Vector-borne disease: dengue, chikungunya, filaria, kala-azar",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Blood samples for microfilariae in bancroftian filariasis should be collected:",
   "options": [
    "Any time",
    "At noon",
    "At night, between 10 pm and 2 am, because of nocturnal periodicity",
    "Early morning"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Wuchereria bancrofti microfilariae show nocturnal periodicity, appearing in peripheral blood at night coinciding with the vector's biting habit. A DEC provocation test allows daytime sampling if necessary.",
