   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Chikungunya is distinguished clinically from dengue by:",
   "options": [
    "Severe thrombocytopenia",
    "Severe and often prolonged incapacitating polyarthralgia with a low risk of haemorrhage or shock",
    "High mortality",
    "Plasma leakage"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Both are Aedes-borne with similar acute fever and rash, but chikungunya causes disabling symmetrical small joint arthralgia persisting for months, while plasma leakage, shock and marked thrombocytopenia point to dengue.",
