   "concept": "Endotoxin is the lipid A of the Gram-negative outer membrane, released on lysis, heat stable and causing fever, hypotension and disseminated intravascular coagulation. Exotoxins are secreted proteins, highly potent, antigenic and convertible to toxoids for vaccines.",
