   "topic": "Bacterial structure, growth, genetics & antimicrobial resistance",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Plasmids differ from bacterial chromosomes in that they:",
   "options": [
    "Are extrachromosomal, self-replicating and non-essential for survival",
    "Are essential for survival",
    "Cannot be transferred",
    "Are always integrated"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Plasmids carry accessory genes for antibiotic resistance, toxin production and virulence, replicating independently and transferable by conjugation - the principal vehicle for the spread of multidrug resistance.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Bacterial Genetics",
