   "topic": "Herpesviruses, CMV & EBV",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The characteristic feature of all herpesviruses is:",
   "options": [
    "Absence of an envelope",
    "Inability to cause recurrence",
    "RNA genome",
    "Ability to establish lifelong latency with periodic reactivation"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Herpesviruses are enveloped DNA viruses that persist lifelong - HSV and VZV in sensory ganglia, EBV in B lymphocytes, CMV in monocytes - reactivating with stress, immunosuppression or ageing.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Herpesviruses",
   "tags": [
