   "topic": "Herpesviruses, CMV & EBV",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Herpes simplex encephalitis characteristically involves:",
   "options": [
    "The spinal cord",
    "The occipital lobes",
    "The temporal lobes, causing haemorrhagic necrosis",
    "The cerebellum"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "HSV-1 encephalitis produces temporal lobe haemorrhagic necrosis with fever, behavioural change, aphasia and seizures. It is the commonest sporadic fatal encephalitis; CSF PCR is diagnostic and intravenous acyclovir must be started empirically.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Herpesviruses",
