   "topic": "Herpesviruses, CMV & EBV",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Infectious mononucleosis caused by Epstein-Barr virus is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Negative heterophile antibodies always",
    "Neutrophilia",
    "Absent lymphadenopathy",
    "Fever, pharyngitis, lymphadenopathy with atypical lymphocytes and a positive Paul-Bunnell test"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "EBV infects B cells via CD21; the atypical lymphocytes (Downey cells) are reactive T cells. Ampicillin given in error produces a florid maculopapular rash, and splenic rupture is a feared complication.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Herpesviruses",
   "tags": [
