   "topic": "Herpesviruses, CMV & EBV",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Roseola infantum (exanthem subitum) with high fever followed by rash as the fever settles is caused by:",
   "options": [
    "Measles virus",
    "Rubella virus",
    "Human herpesvirus 6",
    "Parvovirus B19"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "HHV-6 causes three to five days of high fever in infants, often with febrile convulsions, followed by a maculopapular rash appearing as the temperature falls - the sequence that distinguishes it from measles.",
