   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Treponema pallidum is best visualised by:",
   "options": [
    "Routine culture",
    "Dark ground microscopy of exudate from a lesion",
    "Gram stain",
    "Ziehl-Neelsen stain"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "T. pallidum is too slender to be seen on Gram stain and cannot be cultured on artificial media, so dark ground microscopy showing corkscrew motility, or PCR and serology, are used.",
