   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "VDRL and RPR tests for syphilis are:",
   "options": [
    "Non-treponemal tests useful for screening and monitoring treatment response",
    "Specific for treponemes",
    "Unaffected by treatment",
    "Confirmatory tests"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Non-treponemal tests detect antibody to cardiolipin, become negative after successful treatment and so track response, but give biological false positives in pregnancy, SLE, leprosy and malaria. TPHA and FTA-ABS confirm and stay positive for life.",
