   "topic": "Spirochaetes: syphilis, leptospira, borrelia",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The prozone phenomenon in VDRL testing causes:",
   "options": [
    "Increased sensitivity",
    "No effect",
    "A false positive",
    "A false negative result due to antibody excess in secondary syphilis"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Excess antibody prevents lattice formation, giving a falsely negative undiluted test; serial dilution of the serum reveals the true positive. It occurs classically in secondary syphilis when titres are highest.",
