   "topic": "Rabies, polio & enteroviruses",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Post-exposure prophylaxis for a category III rabies exposure requires:",
   "options": [
    "Immunoglobulin alone",
    "Observation of the animal only",
    "Vaccine alone",
    "Thorough wound washing, rabies immunoglobulin infiltrated into the wound, and a full vaccine course"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Category III means transdermal bites, scratches with bleeding or mucosal contamination, requiring immediate washing with soap and water for 15 minutes, local infiltration of immunoglobulin and vaccination. Category II needs washing and vaccine only.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Rabies",
   "tags": [
