   "topic": "Rabies, polio & enteroviruses",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The intradermal rabies vaccination regimen is preferred in India because it:",
   "options": [
    "Does not need immunoglobulin",
    "Requires fewer visits",
    "Uses less vaccine at lower cost with equivalent immunogenicity",
    "Is more immunogenic"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Intradermal regimens use one-fifth of the intramuscular dose per site, greatly reducing cost in a high-burden setting, and are endorsed by WHO. Immunoglobulin is still required for category III exposures.",
