   "topic": "Rabies, polio & enteroviruses",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Poliovirus is transmitted principally by:",
   "options": [
    "Vector bites",
    "Blood transfusion",
    "The faeco-oral route",
    "Droplet inhalation"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Poliovirus replicates in the oropharynx and gut, spreading faeco-orally, so sanitation and immunisation are central to control. Fewer than 1% of infections cause paralytic disease, which is why surveillance depends on acute flaccid paralysis reporting.",
