   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Rabies, polio & enteroviruses",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The advantage of oral polio vaccine over inactivated vaccine in an endemic setting is that it:",
   "options": [
    "Requires no cold chain",
    "Is more heat stable",
    "Induces gut mucosal immunity and provides contact immunity to unvaccinated persons",
    "Is safer"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "OPV produces secretory IgA in the intestine interrupting wild virus transmission, and vaccine virus spreads to close contacts extending herd protection. IPV produces excellent humoral but limited intestinal immunity.",
