   "topic": "Helminths: intestinal & tissue nematodes, cestodes, trematodes",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The drug of choice for most intestinal nematode infections is:",
   "options": [
    "Albendazole",
    "Metronidazole",
    "Ivermectin",
    "Praziquantel"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Albendazole and mebendazole inhibit tubulin polymerisation and cover ascaris, hookworm, whipworm and pinworm - the basis of mass deworming. Praziquantel is used for cestodes and trematodes, ivermectin for strongyloides and onchocerciasis.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Anthelmintics",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield",
