   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Helminths: intestinal & tissue nematodes, cestodes, trematodes",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Cysticercosis of the eye is important because:",
   "options": [
    "It is untreatable",
    "Antihelminthic treatment can provoke severe inflammation and blindness, so ocular disease must be excluded first",
    "It never occurs",
    "It resolves spontaneously"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Killing an intraocular cyst releases antigens causing intense uveitis, so fundoscopy is mandatory before starting albendazole for neurocysticercosis, and corticosteroids are given alongside to limit inflammation.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Cestodes",
   "tags": [
