   "topic": "Muscle relaxants, monitoring, anaesthesia machine & breathing circuits",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Pulse oximetry gives falsely normal readings in:",
   "options": [
    "Hypotension",
    "Hypothermia",
    "Carbon monoxide poisoning",
    "Anaemia"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Carboxyhaemoglobin absorbs light similarly to oxyhaemoglobin, so saturation appears normal despite severe tissue hypoxia; co-oximetry is required. Methaemoglobinaemia drives the reading towards 85% regardless of true saturation.",
   "reference": "Morgan & Mikhail's Clinical Anesthesiology 6e, Ch. Patient Monitors",
   "tags": [
