   "topic": "Muscle relaxants, monitoring, anaesthesia machine & breathing circuits",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Soda lime in the circle absorber removes carbon dioxide and is exhausted when:",
   "options": [
    "The canister feels cold",
    "The indicator dye changes colour and inspired carbon dioxide rises",
    "Pressure rises",
    "Oxygen falls"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Soda lime, mainly calcium hydroxide with sodium hydroxide, generates heat and moisture as it absorbs carbon dioxide; ethyl violet indicator changes colour on exhaustion. Rising inspired carbon dioxide on capnography confirms it.",
   "reference": "Morgan & Mikhail's Clinical Anesthesiology 6e, Ch. Breathing Systems",
