   "topic": "Muscle relaxants, monitoring, anaesthesia machine & breathing circuits",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The train-of-four ratio is used to assess:",
   "options": [
    "Analgesia",
    "Cardiac output",
    "Adequacy of neuromuscular blockade and its reversal",
    "Depth of anaesthesia"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Four supramaximal stimuli at 2 Hz produce progressive fade with non-depolarising block; a ratio above 0.9 indicates adequate recovery for safe extubation. Depolarising block shows uniform reduction without fade.",
