   "topic": "Regional, spinal & epidural anaesthesia; postoperative care, pain & complications",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Spinal anaesthesia is administered into the subarachnoid space below which vertebral level to avoid cord injury?",
   "options": [
    "L2 in adults",
    "T12",
    "L5 only",
    "S1"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "The spinal cord ends at L1-L2 in adults and L3 in infants, so injection is made at L3-4 or L4-5, identified by Tuffier's line joining the iliac crests.",
   "reference": "Morgan & Mikhail's Clinical Anesthesiology 6e, Ch. Spinal Anesthesia",
   "tags": [
