   "topic": "Regional, spinal & epidural anaesthesia; postoperative care, pain & complications",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The commonest complication of spinal anaesthesia is:",
   "options": [
    "Total spinal",
    "Nerve injury",
    "Hypotension from sympathetic blockade",
    "Meningitis"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Sympathetic block causes vasodilatation with hypotension and bradycardia if cardioaccelerator fibres at T1-T4 are involved, managed by fluid preloading, vasopressors and left lateral tilt in pregnancy.",
