   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Regional, spinal & epidural anaesthesia; postoperative care, pain & complications",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Cauda equina syndrome after spinal anaesthesia has been associated with:",
   "options": [
    "Continuous spinal microcatheters with concentrated hyperbaric lignocaine",
    "Adrenaline",
    "Single-shot technique",
    "Bupivacaine at standard dose"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Maldistribution with pooling of concentrated local anaesthetic around sacral roots causes bowel, bladder and sensory deficits. Concentrated lignocaine for spinal use has therefore been largely abandoned.",
   "reference": "Morgan & Mikhail's Clinical Anesthesiology 6e, Ch. Spinal Anesthesia",
   "tags": [
