   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Munchausen syndrome is classified as:",
   "options": [
    "Somatisation",
    "Factitious disorder, in which symptoms are intentionally produced to assume the sick role",
    "Malingering for money",
    "Conversion disorder"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The motivation is internal - to be a patient - rather than external gain, distinguishing it from malingering. Munchausen by proxy, where a carer fabricates illness in a child, is a form of child abuse.",
   "reference": "Kaplan & Sadock's Synopsis of Psychiatry 12e, Ch. Factitious Disorders",
