   "topic": "Somatoform, dissociative, personality & sexual disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Borderline personality disorder is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Perfectionism",
    "Social withdrawal",
    "Unstable relationships, identity disturbance, impulsivity and recurrent self-harm",
    "Grandiosity"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Cluster B borderline personality shows affective instability, fear of abandonment, chronic emptiness and self-harm. Dialectical behaviour therapy is the treatment with the best evidence.",
