   "topic": "Somatoform, dissociative, personality & sexual disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Antisocial personality disorder requires evidence of:",
   "options": [
    "Psychotic features",
    "Onset after 40",
    "Conduct disorder before age 15 with a persistent disregard for the rights of others",
    "Anxiety symptoms"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Diagnosis requires the individual to be at least 18 with evidence of conduct disorder in childhood, showing deceitfulness, impulsivity, aggression, irresponsibility and lack of remorse. It responds poorly to treatment.",
   "reference": "Kaplan & Sadock's Synopsis of Psychiatry 12e, Ch. Personality Disorders",
