   "topic": "Somatoform, dissociative, personality & sexual disorders",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Cluster A personality disorders (paranoid, schizoid, schizotypal) are best described as:",
   "options": [
    "Odd and eccentric",
    "Dramatic and erratic",
    "Anxious and fearful",
    "Obsessional"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Cluster A is odd or eccentric, cluster B dramatic, emotional or erratic (antisocial, borderline, histrionic, narcissistic), and cluster C anxious or fearful (avoidant, dependent, obsessive-compulsive personality).",
   "reference": "Kaplan & Sadock's Synopsis of Psychiatry 12e, Ch. Personality Disorders",
   "tags": [
