   "topic": "Innate & adaptive immunity, antigen-antibody reactions, vaccines",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The immunoglobulin present in highest concentration in serum is:",
   "options": [
    "IgE",
    "IgM",
    "IgG",
    "IgA"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "IgG constitutes about 75% of serum immunoglobulin, is the only class crossing the placenta giving passive neonatal immunity, and predominates in the secondary response. IgA predominates in secretions and IgM in the primary response.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Immunology",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_MIC_IMM_002",
   "part": "A",
   "subject": "Microbiology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Innate & adaptive immunity, antigen-antibody reactions, vaccines",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The first antibody produced in a primary immune response is:",
   "options": [
    "IgA",
    "IgG",
    "IgE",
    "IgM, a pentamer and the most efficient complement activator"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "IgM appears first and its pentameric structure makes it the best agglutinator and complement fixer. Detecting specific IgM therefore indicates recent or acute infection, as in dengue or hepatitis A.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Immunology",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield",
    "#PYQ"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
