   "topic": "Innate & adaptive immunity, antigen-antibody reactions, vaccines",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The cold chain is required for vaccines because:",
   "options": [
    "It prevents contamination",
    "It is a legal formality",
    "Heat and, for some vaccines, freezing destroy potency",
    "Cold increases potency"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "OPV and measles are the most heat-sensitive, while DPT, hepatitis B and TT are damaged by freezing and must never be frozen - a common field error detected by the shake test.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Cold Chain",
