   "topic": "Innate & adaptive immunity, antigen-antibody reactions, vaccines",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Natural killer cells differ from cytotoxic T cells in that they:",
   "options": [
    "Are antibody-producing",
    "Are part of adaptive immunity",
    "Kill without prior sensitisation and are inhibited by MHC class I",
    "Require MHC presentation"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "NK cells detect missing self - loss of MHC class I on virus-infected or tumour cells - and also kill via antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity through CD16, bridging innate and adaptive immunity.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Immunology",
