   "topic": "Arboviruses: dengue, chikungunya, JE, Zika",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Japanese encephalitis is maintained in nature by a cycle involving:",
   "options": [
    "Pigs as amplifying hosts and ardeid birds as reservoirs, with Culex vectors",
    "Dogs as reservoir",
    "Rodents as reservoir",
    "Humans as reservoir"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Humans are dead-end hosts with low viraemia, so control targets vector reduction, pig management away from dwellings and vaccination in endemic districts. Culex tritaeniorhynchus breeds in rice fields.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Japanese Encephalitis",
   "tags": [
