   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Arboviruses: dengue, chikungunya, JE, Zika",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The tourniquet (Hess) test in dengue assesses:",
   "options": [
    "Capillary fragility, becoming positive with 10 or more petechiae per square inch",
    "Coagulation factors",
    "Plasma leakage volume",
    "Platelet count"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Inflating a cuff to midway between systolic and diastolic pressure for five minutes and counting petechiae in a 2.5 cm square gives a simple bedside indicator of capillary fragility, though it is neither sensitive nor specific.",
