   "topic": "Arboviruses: dengue, chikungunya, JE, Zika",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Aedes aegypti control is difficult in urban India because the mosquito:",
   "options": [
    "Has a long flight range",
    "Breeds in dirty drains",
    "Bites only at night",
    "Breeds in small clean water collections in and around houses and bites during the day"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Domestic breeding in coolers, tyres, tanks and flowerpots means control depends on community-based source reduction rather than spraying alone, and daytime biting makes bed nets largely ineffective.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Dengue",
