   "topic": "Arboviruses: dengue, chikungunya, JE, Zika",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Chikungunya differs from dengue clinically by causing:",
   "options": [
    "Marked plasma leakage",
    "Severe thrombocytopenia",
    "Severe persistent symmetrical polyarthralgia lasting weeks to months",
    "High mortality"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Both are transmitted by Aedes with overlapping acute features, but chikungunya causes disabling arthralgia that may persist for months, while dengue causes plasma leakage, shock and haemorrhage.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Chikungunya",
