   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Specimen collection, serology & molecular diagnostics",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "In suspected enteric fever, the specimen with the highest yield in the first week of illness is:",
   "options": [
    "Blood culture",
    "Stool culture",
    "Urine culture",
    "Widal test"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Blood culture is positive in about 80% in week one, stool and urine cultures become positive in the second and third weeks, and bone marrow culture has the highest yield overall and remains positive despite antibiotics.",
