   "topic": "Specimen collection, serology & molecular diagnostics",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Cerebrospinal fluid for suspected bacterial meningitis must be:",
   "options": [
    "Refrigerated",
    "Transported immediately at room temperature and never refrigerated",
    "Stored for 24 hours",
    "Frozen"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Meningococcus and Haemophilus are highly susceptible to cold and drying, so refrigeration kills them. CSF is processed urgently with Gram stain, cell count, biochemistry and culture, plus latex agglutination or PCR.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Laboratory Diagnosis",
   "tags": [
