   "topic": "Cornea: keratitis, ulcers, dystrophies & corneal transplant",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A corneal ulcer with feathery margins and satellite lesions in a farmer after injury with vegetative matter suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Exposure keratitis",
    "Bacterial keratitis",
    "Fungal keratitis",
    "Viral keratitis"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Fusarium and Aspergillus keratitis follows vegetative trauma, showing dry raised ulcers with feathery edges, satellite lesions and an immune ring. Natamycin is first line; steroids are strictly contraindicated.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Cornea",
   "tags": [
