   "topic": "Cornea: keratitis, ulcers, dystrophies & corneal transplant",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Severe pain out of proportion to signs with a ring infiltrate in a contact lens wearer suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Acanthamoeba keratitis",
    "Herpes zoster",
    "Bacterial ulcer",
    "Dry eye"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Acanthamoeba is associated with contact lens use and exposure to contaminated water, causing disproportionate pain, radial keratoneuritis and a ring infiltrate. Diagnosis is by confocal microscopy or culture on non-nutrient agar with E. coli.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Cornea",
   "tags": [
