    "Sterile inflammatory exudate settling in the anterior chamber",
    "Pus containing organisms",
    "Lens material",
    "Blood"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Hypopyon in bacterial keratitis is usually sterile, resulting from toxin-driven inflammation with an intact Descemet membrane, so intraocular tap is not routinely needed. It indicates severe disease requiring intensive therapy.",
