   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A Kayser-Fleischer ring is deposition of copper in:",
   "options": [
    "The epithelium",
    "The endothelium centrally",
    "The stroma centrally",
    "Descemet membrane at the corneal periphery"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Copper deposits in Descemet membrane produce a golden-brown peripheral ring best seen on gonioscopy, and is a diagnostic feature of Wilson disease, often accompanied by a sunflower cataract.",
