   "topic": "Cornea: keratitis, ulcers, dystrophies & corneal transplant",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Vitamin A deficiency causing corneal melting and perforation is termed:",
   "options": [
    "Bitot spot",
    "Xerophthalmia only",
    "Nyctalopia",
    "Keratomalacia"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Keratomalacia is the end stage of xerophthalmia, a blinding emergency in malnourished children requiring immediate high-dose vitamin A. The sequence runs night blindness, conjunctival xerosis, Bitot spots, corneal xerosis, ulceration then keratomalacia.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Vitamin A Deficiency",
