   "topic": "Conjunctiva, lids & lacrimal apparatus",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A stye (hordeolum externum) is an acute infection of:",
   "options": [
    "The meibomian gland",
    "The conjunctiva",
    "The lacrimal gland",
    "The gland of Zeis or Moll at the lid margin"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "An external hordeolum is a staphylococcal abscess of the lash follicle and its associated glands, treated with hot compresses, lash epilation and topical antibiotics. Internal hordeolum involves the meibomian gland.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Diseases of the Eyelids",
