   "topic": "Conjunctiva, lids & lacrimal apparatus",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A chalazion is:",
   "options": [
    "A malignant tumour",
    "An acute abscess",
    "A chronic non-infective lipogranuloma of the meibomian gland",
    "A viral lesion"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Blocked meibomian secretion produces a painless firm nodule away from the lid margin. Incision and curettage from the conjunctival surface is standard; a recurrent chalazion in the elderly warrants biopsy to exclude sebaceous carcinoma.",
