    "Viral conjunctivitis",
    "Bacterial conjunctivitis",
    "Trachoma"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Vernal catarrh is a seasonal type I and IV hypersensitivity of young boys, with intense itching, ropy discharge, giant papillae and limbal Horner-Trantas dots. Mast cell stabilisers are the mainstay, steroids used sparingly.",
