   "stem": "Endophthalmitis following cataract surgery most commonly presents:",
   "options": [
    "With itching only",
    "Painlessly",
    "Within a few days with pain, reduced vision and hypopyon",
    "After one year"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Acute postoperative endophthalmitis, usually from coagulase-negative staphylococci, is a sight-threatening emergency requiring urgent vitreous tap with intravitreal antibiotics. Delayed onset suggests Propionibacterium acnes.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Uveal Tract",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_OP_UVE_009",
