   "topic": "Uveitis, scleritis & ocular inflammation",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Cytomegalovirus retinitis in advanced HIV appears as:",
   "options": [
    "Pizza-pie fundus with haemorrhage and necrosis along vessels",
    "A pale optic disc",
    "Retinal detachment only",
    "Vitreous haemorrhage"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "CMV retinitis occurs at CD4 counts below 50, producing the characteristic brushfire or pizza-pie appearance of white necrosis with haemorrhage. Treatment is ganciclovir or valganciclovir with antiretroviral therapy.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Retina",
   "tags": [
