   "topic": "Retina & vitreous: vascular occlusions, ARMD, retinoblastoma",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A blood-and-thunder fundus with flame haemorrhages in all quadrants indicates:",
   "options": [
    "Hypertensive retinopathy",
    "Diabetic retinopathy",
    "Central retinal vein occlusion",
    "Central retinal artery occlusion"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Venous obstruction causes widespread haemorrhages, dilated tortuous veins, cotton wool spots and disc oedema. The ischaemic type risks neovascular glaucoma at about 90 days - hence the term hundred-day glaucoma.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Retina",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
