   "topic": "Diabetic retinopathy, retinal detachment",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The hallmark of proliferative diabetic retinopathy is:",
   "options": [
    "Neovascularisation of the disc or elsewhere",
    "Hard exudates",
    "Microaneurysms",
    "Dot-blot haemorrhages"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "New vessels from retinal ischaemia bleed into the vitreous and cause tractional detachment. Panretinal photocoagulation and anti-VEGF therapy are the treatments; the earlier changes are non-proliferative.",
