   "topic": "Retina & vitreous: vascular occlusions, ARMD, retinoblastoma",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Age-related macular degeneration typically causes:",
   "options": [
    "Night blindness only",
    "Progressive loss of central vision with preserved peripheral vision",
    "Sudden total blindness",
    "Loss of peripheral vision"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Macular involvement destroys central acuity for reading and faces while navigational peripheral vision is retained. Dry ARMD shows drusen and atrophy; wet ARMD has choroidal neovascularisation treated with intravitreal anti-VEGF.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Retina",
   "tags": [
