   "topic": "Retina & vitreous: vascular occlusions, ARMD, retinoblastoma",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Retinitis pigmentosa classically presents with:",
   "options": [
    "Sudden painless loss",
    "Night blindness with progressive constriction of visual fields and bone-spicule pigmentation",
    "Painful red eye",
    "Central vision loss first"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Rod degeneration causes nyctalopia and ring scotoma progressing to tunnel vision, with waxy disc pallor, attenuated arterioles and perivascular bone-spicule pigment, and an extinguished electroretinogram.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Retina",
   "tags": [
