   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Papilloedema is distinguished from papillitis by:",
   "options": [
    "Marked early acuity loss",
    "Preserved visual acuity in papilloedema despite a swollen disc",
    "Pain on eye movement",
    "Unilateral involvement"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Papilloedema from raised intracranial pressure is bilateral with normal acuity, enlarged blind spot and no pain, whereas papillitis is usually unilateral with marked acuity loss, a relative afferent pupillary defect and pain on movement.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Neuro-ophthalmology",
   "tags": [
