   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Amblyopia is best defined as:",
   "options": [
    "Reduced vision in a structurally normal eye due to abnormal visual development",
    "Optic atrophy",
    "Loss of vision from retinal disease",
    "Corneal opacity"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Amblyopia results from form deprivation, strabismus or anisometropia during the critical period. Treatment by correcting refraction and occluding the better eye is effective only if started early, usually before 7 to 8 years.",
