   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The Hirschberg corneal reflex test is used to:",
   "options": [
    "Estimate the angle of deviation in squint",
    "Measure visual acuity",
    "Assess colour vision",
    "Measure intraocular pressure"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "A torch reflex displaced from the pupil centre estimates deviation, with each millimetre corresponding to about 7 degrees. The cover-uncover test distinguishes manifest tropia from latent phoria.",
