   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A lesion at the optic chiasm characteristically produces:",
   "options": [
    "Altitudinal defect",
    "Homonymous hemianopia",
    "Bitemporal hemianopia",
    "Central scotoma"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Decussating nasal retinal fibres carrying temporal fields are damaged, classically by a pituitary adenoma extending upward, beginning in the upper temporal quadrants. Lesions behind the chiasm cause homonymous defects.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Neuro-ophthalmology",
   "tags": [
