   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A right homonymous hemianopia with macular sparing suggests a lesion of:",
   "options": [
    "The left occipital cortex",
    "The chiasm",
    "The right optic tract",
    "The right optic nerve"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Macular sparing reflects dual blood supply of the occipital pole by middle and posterior cerebral arteries, so posterior cerebral artery infarction spares central vision. Congruity increases the more posterior the lesion.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Neuro-ophthalmology",
   "tags": [
