   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "An Argyll Robertson pupil is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "A dilated fixed pupil",
    "A small irregular pupil that accommodates but does not react to light",
    "Normal reactions",
    "A constricted reactive pupil"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Classically associated with neurosyphilis, it shows light-near dissociation with bilateral small irregular pupils. The Adie tonic pupil is instead large with slow tonic near response and absent tendon reflexes.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Neuro-ophthalmology",
   "tags": [
