   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Optic neuritis in a young woman with pain on eye movement and a central scotoma should prompt evaluation for:",
   "options": [
    "Cataract",
    "Glaucoma",
    "Diabetes",
    "Multiple sclerosis"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Optic neuritis is often the presenting feature of multiple sclerosis, and MRI showing periventricular white matter lesions predicts conversion. Intravenous methylprednisolone speeds recovery but does not alter final acuity.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Neuro-ophthalmology",
