   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Fourth cranial nerve palsy characteristically causes:",
   "options": [
    "Loss of abduction",
    "Horizontal diplopia",
    "Ptosis",
    "Vertical diplopia worse on looking down, with compensatory head tilt to the opposite side"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Superior oblique palsy impairs depression in adduction, so patients tilt the head away from the affected side (positive Bielschowsky test) and struggle going downstairs or reading.",
