   "topic": "Squint, amblyopia & neuro-ophthalmology (optic nerve, pupil, fields)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Pseudosquint in an Indian child is most often due to:",
   "options": [
    "Cataract",
    "Retinoblastoma",
    "Prominent epicanthal folds giving an appearance of esotropia with normal corneal reflexes",
    "True muscle imbalance"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Epicanthal folds obscure the nasal sclera creating an illusion of convergent squint, but corneal reflexes are symmetrical and cover test is normal. Any true squint after 6 months of age requires prompt referral.",
