   "topic": "Ocular trauma, orbit, ocular pharmacology & blindness control",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The immediate first aid for a chemical burn of the eye is:",
   "options": [
    "Copious irrigation with clean water or saline before any other assessment",
    "Topical steroid",
    "Padding the eye",
    "Referral without irrigation"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Immediate prolonged irrigation is the single most important determinant of outcome and must precede history-taking and acuity measurement. Alkali burns penetrate deeper by saponification and are more damaging than acids.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Ocular Injuries",
