   "topic": "Ocular trauma, orbit, ocular pharmacology & blindness control",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A blowout fracture of the orbital floor characteristically causes:",
   "options": [
    "Loss of vision only",
    "Proptosis",
    "Diplopia on upgaze with enophthalmos and infraorbital anaesthesia",
    "Ptosis alone"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Entrapment of inferior rectus and orbital fat in the maxillary sinus restricts elevation, and infraorbital nerve injury causes cheek numbness. CT shows the teardrop sign of herniated contents.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Ocular Injuries",
