   "topic": "Ocular trauma, orbit, ocular pharmacology & blindness control",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Hyphaema after blunt ocular trauma is managed by:",
   "options": [
    "Aspirin for pain",
    "Vigorous activity",
    "Rest with head elevation, monitoring intraocular pressure, and avoiding aspirin",
    "Immediate surgery"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Most hyphaemas resorb spontaneously; the risks are secondary rebleeding around days 3 to 5, raised intraocular pressure and corneal blood staining. Aspirin and NSAIDs are avoided as they promote rebleeding.",
   "reference": "AK Khurana Comprehensive Ophthalmology 8e, Ch. Ocular Injuries",
   "tags": [
