   "topic": "Ocular trauma, orbit, ocular pharmacology & blindness control",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Retrobulbar haemorrhage after injury or block presents with:",
   "options": [
    "Gradual visual loss",
    "Painless proptosis",
    "Proptosis, tense orbit, raised intraocular pressure and threatened vision requiring urgent canthotomy",
    "Ptosis alone"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "This orbital compartment syndrome compromises the optic nerve blood supply within minutes, requiring immediate lateral canthotomy and cantholysis at the bedside rather than transfer for imaging.",
