   "topic": "Ocular trauma, orbit, ocular pharmacology & blindness control",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Topical timolol is contraindicated in:",
   "options": [
    "Hypertension",
    "Cataract",
    "Asthma and heart block",
    "Diabetes"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Even topical beta blockers are systemically absorbed through the nasolacrimal duct, precipitating bronchospasm and bradycardia. Punctal occlusion reduces absorption; prostaglandin analogues are safer alternatives.",
