   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The commonest direction of shoulder dislocation is:",
   "options": [
    "Anterior",
    "Posterior",
    "Inferior",
    "Superior"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Over 95% are anterior, from abduction and external rotation, giving a flattened deltoid contour with the arm held abducted. The axillary nerve must be tested for sensation over the regimental badge area before and after reduction.",
   "reference": "Maheshwari Essential Orthopaedics 6e, Ch. Upper Limb Injuries",
   "tags": [
