   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Specific fractures (Colles, NOF, supracondylar) & healing",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A Colles fracture is a fracture of the distal radius with:",
   "options": [
    "No displacement",
    "Radial shortening only",
    "Dorsal displacement and angulation producing a dinner-fork deformity",
    "Volar displacement"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Colles fracture follows a fall on the outstretched hand in an osteoporotic patient, with dorsal tilt, dorsal shift, radial shift and supination. A Smith fracture is the volar-displaced reverse injury.",
   "reference": "Maheshwari Essential Orthopaedics 6e, Ch. Upper Limb Injuries",
   "tags": [
