   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The nerve most commonly injured in a fracture of the shaft of the humerus is:",
   "options": [
    "Radial nerve, causing wrist drop",
    "Median nerve",
    "Ulnar nerve",
    "Axillary nerve"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "The radial nerve lies in the spiral groove against the humerus and is injured in about 10% of shaft fractures. Most are neuropraxias recovering spontaneously, so initial management is conservative with a splint.",
   "reference": "Maheshwari Essential Orthopaedics 6e, Ch. Upper Limb Injuries",
   "tags": [
