   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A Monteggia fracture-dislocation consists of:",
   "options": [
    "Isolated radial head fracture",
    "Fracture of both bones",
    "Fracture of the distal radius with distal radioulnar dislocation",
    "Fracture of the proximal ulna with dislocation of the radial head"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Monteggia is ulnar fracture with radial head dislocation; Galeazzi is radial shaft fracture with distal radioulnar joint disruption. In any single forearm bone fracture the joints above and below must be imaged.",
