   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Carpal tunnel syndrome causes sensory loss over:",
   "options": [
    "The dorsum only",
    "The lateral three and a half digits, sparing the thenar eminence",
    "The medial one and a half digits",
    "The whole hand"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The palmar cutaneous branch arises proximal to the flexor retinaculum, so thenar skin sensation is spared - the key sign distinguishing carpal tunnel compression from a proximal median nerve lesion.",
