   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Injury to the ulnar nerve at the elbow produces:",
   "options": [
    "A more severe claw",
    "Wrist drop",
    "Claw hand that is less deforming than a distal lesion, due to the ulnar paradox",
    "No deformity"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "A proximal lesion also paralyses flexor digitorum profundus to the ring and little fingers, so those fingers cannot flex at the DIP joints and the claw is less marked - the ulnar paradox.",
   "reference": "Maheshwari Essential Orthopaedics 6e, Ch. Peripheral Nerve Lesions",
