   "topic": "Upper limb injuries: shoulder, humerus, elbow, wrist",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Recurrent anterior shoulder dislocation is associated with:",
   "options": [
    "A Bankart lesion of the anteroinferior labrum and a Hill-Sachs defect of the humeral head",
    "Acromioclavicular injury",
    "Clavicle fracture",
    "A rotator cuff tear only"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Detachment of the anteroinferior labrum with capsular stripping predisposes to recurrence, and impaction of the posterolateral humeral head against the glenoid rim creates the Hill-Sachs defect. Arthroscopic Bankart repair is the treatment.",
   "reference": "Maheshwari Essential Orthopaedics 6e, Ch. Upper Limb Injuries",
