   "topic": "Lower limb & pelvic injuries; hip dislocation",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A patient with a shortened, adducted and internally rotated lower limb after a dashboard injury has:",
   "options": [
    "Anterior dislocation of the hip",
    "Pelvic fracture",
    "Posterior dislocation of the hip",
    "Fracture neck of femur"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Posterior dislocation accounts for about 90% of hip dislocations and is an orthopaedic emergency; reduction within 6 hours minimises avascular necrosis. Sciatic nerve injury occurs in about 10%.",
