   "topic": "Lower limb & pelvic injuries; hip dislocation",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The commonest mechanism of ankle injury producing a lateral malleolar fracture is:",
   "options": [
    "Eversion alone",
    "Axial loading",
    "Inversion and supination",
    "Direct anterior blow"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "The Weber classification relates the fibular fracture to the syndesmosis: Weber A below, B at, and C above the level, with C implying syndesmotic disruption needing fixation. Ottawa ankle rules guide the need for radiography.",
