   "topic": "Lower limb & pelvic injuries; hip dislocation",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The unhappy triad of knee injury consists of:",
   "options": [
    "PCL, MCL and medial meniscus",
    "ACL, LCL and lateral meniscus",
    "ACL, PCL and patella",
    "Anterior cruciate ligament, medial collateral ligament and medial meniscus injury"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "A valgus force with external rotation on a planted foot injures all three structures. The anterior drawer and Lachman tests assess the ACL, and McMurray test the menisci.",
