   "topic": "Specific fractures (Colles, NOF, supracondylar) & healing",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "In a suspected femoral neck fracture with normal radiographs, the next investigation is:",
   "options": [
    "MRI of the hip",
    "CT only",
    "Bone scan immediately",
    "Repeat radiograph after two weeks"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "MRI detects occult fractures within hours with the highest sensitivity, avoiding the delay of repeat films or the reduced early sensitivity of bone scanning - important as delayed diagnosis worsens outcomes in the elderly.",
