    "L1-L2",
    "L2-L3"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The lower lumbar levels bear the greatest mechanical load. A posterolateral L4-5 prolapse compresses the L5 root causing weak great toe dorsiflexion, and L5-S1 compresses S1 with a reduced ankle jerk.",
