   "topic": "Spine injury, disc prolapse & spinal deformity",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Neurogenic claudication of lumbar canal stenosis is distinguished from vascular claudication by:",
   "options": [
    "Absent pulses",
    "Pain at rest only",
    "Relief on sitting or bending forward, with preserved peripheral pulses",
    "Relief on standing still"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Flexion increases canal diameter, so patients report relief on stooping and can cycle further than they can walk. Vascular claudication is relieved simply by stopping, with diminished pulses and a reduced ABPI.",
