   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Molluscum contagiosum is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Scaly plaques",
    "Vesicles",
    "Umbilicated pearly papules caused by a poxvirus",
    "Ulcers"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Dome-shaped umbilicated papules contain a central core of molluscum bodies. Extensive lesions in an adult, particularly on the face, should prompt HIV testing; most resolve spontaneously in immunocompetent children.",
   "reference": "IADVL Textbook of Dermatology 5e, Ch. Viral Infections",
