  {
   "id": "Q_DE_ACN_005",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Dermatology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Acne, rosacea, hair & nail disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Alopecia areata is characterised by:",
   "options": [
    "Scarring alopecia",
    "Diffuse thinning",
    "Well-circumscribed patches of non-scarring hair loss with exclamation mark hairs",
    "Broken hairs from traction"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "An autoimmune attack on the hair bulb produces smooth bald patches with tapered exclamation mark hairs at the margin and nail pitting. It is associated with vitiligo, thyroid disease and atopy, and hair follicles are preserved so regrowth is possible.",
   "reference": "IADVL Textbook of Dermatology 5e, Ch. Hair Disorders",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_DE_ACN_006",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Dermatology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Acne, rosacea, hair & nail disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Telogen effluvium typically occurs:",
   "options": [
    "Only in men",
    "Immediately after stress",
    "Without any trigger",
    "Two to three months after a stressor such as illness, surgery, childbirth or severe weight loss"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "A stressor shifts anagen follicles synchronously into telogen, so shedding is delayed by the telogen duration. It is self-limiting with full recovery once the trigger is removed, and reassurance is the main treatment.",
   "reference": "IADVL Textbook of Dermatology 5e, Ch. Hair Disorders",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_DE_ACN_007",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Dermatology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Acne, rosacea, hair & nail disorders",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Androgenetic alopecia in men is treated with:",
   "options": [
    "Topical minoxidil and oral finasteride",
    "Topical steroids",
    "Antifungals",
    "Antibiotics"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Minoxidil prolongs anagen and finasteride inhibits 5-alpha-reductase reducing dihydrotestosterone. Finasteride is contraindicated in women of childbearing age because of feminisation of a male fetus.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Drugs for Alopecia",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_DE_ACN_008",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Dermatology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Acne, rosacea, hair & nail disorders",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Nail pitting is most characteristically associated with:",
   "options": [
    "Lichen planus",
    "Onychomycosis",
    "Psoriasis and alopecia areata",
    "Iron deficiency"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Psoriatic nails show irregular deep pitting, oil-drop discolouration, onycholysis and subungual hyperkeratosis, while alopecia areata gives fine regular geometric pitting. Lichen planus causes pterygium and nail destruction.",
   "reference": "IADVL Textbook of Dermatology 5e, Ch. Nail Disorders",
   "tags": [
