   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Acne, rosacea, hair & nail disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Scarring (cicatricial) alopecia differs from non-scarring in that:",
   "options": [
    "Hair regrows fully",
    "It is never inflammatory",
    "It is always reversible",
    "Follicular openings are permanently destroyed, so regrowth is impossible"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Loss of follicular ostia on examination indicates permanent destruction, seen in discoid lupus, lichen planopilaris and kerion. Early diagnosis and biopsy are essential to arrest activity before further follicles are lost.",
   "reference": "IADVL Textbook of Dermatology 5e, Ch. Hair Disorders",
