   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The medico-legal significance of vital reaction in a burn is that it:",
   "options": [
    "Establishes identity",
    "Indicates the burn was sustained during life rather than after death",
    "Determines the time of death",
    "Determines the cause of the fire"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Antemortem burns show a red line of hyperaemia, vesicles with high protein and chloride content and inflammatory infiltration, whereas postmortem burns lack these vital reactions - crucial in distinguishing burning to conceal homicide.",
   "reference": "Reddy's The Essentials of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology 34e, Ch. Thermal Deaths",
