   "stem": "The legal limit of blood alcohol concentration for driving in India is:",
   "options": [
    "30 mg per 100 mL of blood",
    "80 mg per 100 mL",
    "50 mg per 100 mL",
    "Zero"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "India sets a stricter limit of 30 mg/100 mL than many countries. Breath analysers give an indirect estimate; blood is the definitive medico-legal sample and must be collected without alcohol-containing antiseptic.",
   "reference": "Reddy's The Essentials of Forensic Medicine and Toxicology 34e, Ch. Alcohol",
   "tags": [
