   "topic": "NSAIDs, analgesics, antipyretics & drugs for gout",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Reye syndrome, an encephalopathy with fatty liver, contraindicates aspirin in:",
   "options": [
    "Diabetics",
    "All adults",
    "Children with viral illness such as varicella or influenza",
    "The elderly"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Aspirin is avoided under 16 years except in Kawasaki disease and rheumatic fever, where the benefit outweighs the small risk. Paracetamol is the antipyretic of choice in children.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. NSAIDs",
   "tags": [
