   "part": "A",
   "subject": "Pharmacology",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Sex hormones, contraceptives, uterine & bone drugs",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Oxytocin differs from ergometrine in that oxytocin:",
   "options": [
    "Causes sustained tetanic contraction",
    "Produces rhythmic contractions with relaxation between, so it can be used before delivery of the fetus",
    "Cannot be given intravenously",
    "Is contraindicated postpartum"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Ergometrine causes sustained tonic contraction and is only used after delivery, and is contraindicated in hypertension and pre-eclampsia. Oxytocin has antidiuretic action, risking water intoxication in high-dose infusions.",
