   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Skeletal muscle relaxants & drugs for Parkinsonism",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Pyridoxine reduces the effect of levodopa when given without carbidopa because it:",
   "options": [
    "Blocks absorption",
    "Is a cofactor for peripheral dopa decarboxylase, increasing peripheral conversion",
    "Is an antagonist",
    "Increases excretion"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Vitamin B6 accelerates peripheral metabolism leaving less levodopa for the brain. With a decarboxylase inhibitor this interaction is largely abolished, so modern combinations are unaffected.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Drugs for Parkinsonism",
   "tags": [
