   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Skeletal muscle relaxants & drugs for Parkinsonism",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Baclofen relieves spasticity by acting as:",
   "options": [
    "A calcium channel blocker",
    "A glycine antagonist",
    "A GABA-B receptor agonist in the spinal cord",
    "A GABA-A agonist"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Baclofen reduces spasticity in multiple sclerosis and spinal injury, and may be given intrathecally for severe cases. Abrupt withdrawal, especially of intrathecal therapy, causes seizures and rebound spasticity.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Skeletal Muscle Relaxants",
   "tags": [
