    "Preventing acetylcholine release at the neuromuscular junction",
    "Destroying the muscle",
    "Acting centrally",
    "Blocking the receptor"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Cleavage of SNARE proteins gives chemical denervation lasting about 3 months until new terminals sprout. It is used for cervical dystonia, blepharospasm, spasticity, achalasia, hyperhidrosis and cosmetically.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Skeletal Muscle Relaxants",
   "tags": [
