   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Skeletal muscle relaxants & drugs for Parkinsonism",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "Dopamine agonists such as pramipexole may be preferred as initial therapy in young patients because they:",
   "options": [
    "Cure the disease",
    "Delay the onset of levodopa-induced dyskinesias",
    "Have no side effects",
    "Are more effective than levodopa"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "They are less potent than levodopa but delay motor complications in younger patients with a long disease course ahead. Impulse control disorders such as pathological gambling are a distinctive adverse effect.",
