    "Enhanced sedation",
    "A disulfiram-like reaction with flushing, vomiting and headache",
    "No interaction",
    "Hepatic failure"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Inhibition of aldehyde dehydrogenase causes acetaldehyde accumulation, so alcohol is avoided during and for 48 hours after therapy. Metronidazole also potentiates warfarin and causes a metallic taste and peripheral neuropathy.",
   "reference": "KD Tripathi Essentials of Medical Pharmacology 8e, Ch. Antiamoebic Drugs",
