   "topic": "Clinical trials, pharmacovigilance, prescription writing & drug schedules",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "An intention-to-treat analysis means:",
   "options": [
    "Dropouts are excluded",
    "Only compliant patients are analysed",
    "Participants are analysed in the group to which they were randomised, regardless of adherence",
    "Groups are reassigned by treatment received"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "ITT preserves the benefits of randomisation and gives a pragmatic estimate of effectiveness. Per-protocol analysis, which excludes non-adherers, reintroduces selection bias and typically overestimates efficacy.",
