   "concept": "The prolonged calcium-mediated plateau gives a refractory period lasting nearly the whole contraction, so cardiac muscle cannot summate or tetanise - an essential protection allowing the heart to fill.",
   "reference": "Ganong's Review of Medical Physiology 26e, Ch. Cardiac Physiology",
