   "topic": "Muscle physiology: skeletal, smooth & cardiac contraction",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Muscle fatigue during sustained exercise is primarily due to:",
   "options": [
    "Loss of calcium stores permanently",
    "Complete ATP depletion",
    "Accumulation of metabolites and impaired excitation-contraction coupling rather than ATP depletion",
    "Nerve failure"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "ATP rarely falls below about 60% of resting levels. Accumulation of inorganic phosphate and hydrogen ions and impaired sarcoplasmic calcium release are the dominant mechanisms in peripheral fatigue.",
   "reference": "Ganong's Review of Medical Physiology 26e, Ch. Muscle Physiology",
