    "The liver",
    "The red marrow of flat bones and proximal ends of long bones",
    "The thymus"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "In fetal life the yolk sac, then liver and spleen are the sites; after birth the marrow takes over, retracting to the axial skeleton by adulthood. Extramedullary haemopoiesis resumes in marrow failure or myelofibrosis.",
