    "Only VIII",
    "II, VII, IX and X with proteins C and S",
    "XI, XII"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Gamma-carboxylation confers calcium-binding capacity. Warfarin inhibits vitamin K epoxide reductase, and the early fall in protein C explains transient hypercoagulability at initiation.",
