    "Thrombin alone",
    "Tissue plasminogen activator and urokinase",
    "Factor XIII",
    "Antithrombin"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Plasmin degrades fibrin producing D-dimers, which is why D-dimer is raised in venous thromboembolism and disseminated intravascular coagulation. Tranexamic acid blocks plasminogen binding to fibrin.",
