    "120 days",
    "30 days",
    "7 days",
    "365 days"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Platelets survive 7 to 10 days and neutrophils only hours in the circulation. The 120-day red cell lifespan underlies the use of HbA1c as a 3-month glycaemic index, which is unreliable in haemolysis.",
