   "topic": "Lung volumes, compliance, V/Q & mechanics of breathing",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Functional residual capacity is the sum of:",
   "options": [
    "Tidal volume and residual volume",
    "Inspiratory capacity and tidal volume",
    "Vital capacity and residual volume",
    "Expiratory reserve volume and residual volume"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "FRC is the resting volume where inward elastic recoil of the lung balances outward recoil of the chest wall. It falls in pregnancy, obesity and supine posture, and rises in emphysema.",
   "reference": "Ganong's Review of Medical Physiology 26e, Ch. Respiration",
   "tags": [
