   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "GIT secretions, motility & absorption",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Vitamin B12 absorption requires intrinsic factor and occurs in:",
   "options": [
    "The terminal ileum",
    "The stomach",
    "The jejunum",
    "The duodenum"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "This is why terminal ileal resection or Crohn disease causes B12 deficiency, whereas iron and folate are absorbed in the duodenum and upper jejunum, explaining the pattern of deficiency after different resections.",
   "reference": "Ganong's Review of Medical Physiology 26e, Ch. Gastrointestinal Physiology",
   "tags": [
