   "topic": "Thyroid, adrenal, pancreas & calcium homeostasis",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Cortisol secretion shows a diurnal rhythm with a peak:",
   "options": [
    "At midnight",
    "No rhythm",
    "In the afternoon",
    "In the early morning around 6 to 8 am"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "The midnight nadir is why a raised late-night salivary cortisol is a sensitive screen for Cushing syndrome, and why replacement is given as a larger morning dose.",
