   "id": "Q_BC_CAN_008",
   "part": "A",
   "subject": "Biochemistry",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Cancer biology, oncogenes & tumour biochemistry",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The p53 protein is described as the guardian of the genome because it:",
   "options": [
    "Promotes growth",
    "Replicates DNA",
    "Arrests the cell cycle at G1/S for repair or triggers apoptosis if damage is irreparable",
    "Forms the spindle"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Loss of p53 permits damaged cells to proliferate. Germline mutation causes Li-Fraumeni syndrome with multiple early cancers, and HPV E6 protein degrades p53 in cervical carcinogenesis.",
