   "id": "Q_BC_CAN_010",
   "part": "A",
   "subject": "Biochemistry",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Cancer biology, oncogenes & tumour biochemistry",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Cancer cachexia is mediated principally by:",
   "options": [
    "Reduced intake alone",
    "Cytokines such as TNF-alpha and IL-6 causing hypermetabolism and proteolysis",
    "Malabsorption alone",
    "Anaemia"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Because it is cytokine-driven rather than simple starvation, cachexia is not reversed by feeding alone. It predicts poor prognosis and reduced tolerance of chemotherapy.",
