   "topic": "Association & causation, bias, confounding, measures of risk",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Relative risk is calculated in which study design?",
   "options": [
    "Case-control study",
    "Cross-sectional study",
    "Cohort study, as incidence can be measured directly",
    "Ecological study"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Case-control studies yield the odds ratio, which approximates relative risk when the disease is rare. Only cohort and experimental designs measure incidence and therefore true risk.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Epidemiology",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield",
