   "concept": "Two doses are required because about 15% do not seroconvert to the first. Vitamin A is given with the second dose and continued six-monthly up to five years.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Immunisation",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_PSM_CHI_006",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Child health programmes, IMNCI & school health",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The vaccines given at birth in the national schedule are:",
   "options": [
    "Rotavirus",
    "BCG, oral polio zero dose and hepatitis B birth dose",
    "Measles",
    "DPT and OPV"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The hepatitis B birth dose must be given within 24 hours to prevent perinatal transmission, and OPV zero dose primes mucosal immunity before the primary series begins at 6 weeks.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Immunisation",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield",
    "#PYQ"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_PSM_CHI_007",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Child health programmes, IMNCI & school health",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Mission Indradhanush was launched to:",
   "options": [
    "Increase full immunisation coverage by reaching unvaccinated and partially vaccinated children",
    "Provide nutrition",
    "Build hospitals",
    "Train nurses"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "It targets districts with low coverage in campaign mode, addressing the reality that dropout between first and later doses, rather than complete non-immunisation, is the main gap.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Immunisation",
   "tags": [
