   "topic": "Non-communicable disease epidemiology: CVD, diabetes, cancer, tobacco",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The most important modifiable risk factor for cardiovascular disease amenable to population intervention is:",
   "options": [
    "Sex",
    "Age",
    "Tobacco use",
    "Family history"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Tobacco, unhealthy diet, physical inactivity and harmful alcohol use are the four shared behavioural risk factors underlying the major non-communicable diseases, making them the focus of population strategies.",
