   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Environmental health: air, noise, housing, climate",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The most effective single method of purifying water at household level is:",
   "options": [
    "Sedimentation",
    "Filtration through cloth",
    "Adding alum",
    "Boiling for 5 to 10 minutes"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Boiling kills all pathogens including cysts and viruses but does not remove chemical contaminants and offers no residual protection against recontamination, which chlorination provides.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Water",
   "tags": [
