   "topic": "Respiratory & vaccine-preventable disease epidemiology (measles, diphtheria, polio)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A case of measles is infectious from:",
   "options": [
    "Two weeks before",
    "Only during the rash",
    "Only after the rash",
    "Four days before to four days after the appearance of rash"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Infectivity begins in the prodrome, so isolation after the rash appears is too late to prevent spread - a key reason measles propagates so efficiently in schools and hospitals.",
