   "topic": "Respiratory & vaccine-preventable disease epidemiology (measles, diphtheria, polio)",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Diphtheria is prevented by:",
   "options": [
    "An antibiotic",
    "A live vaccine",
    "Toxoid, which produces antitoxic rather than antibacterial immunity",
    "Immunoglobulin"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Because immunity is antitoxic, vaccinated persons may still carry the organism, which is why treatment of cases requires antitoxin and antibiotics and contacts require prophylaxis and boosting.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Diphtheria",
   "tags": [
