   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Respiratory & vaccine-preventable disease epidemiology (measles, diphtheria, polio)",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Herd immunity is not applicable to which vaccine-preventable disease?",
   "options": [
    "Diphtheria",
    "Measles",
    "Tetanus, because it is acquired from the environment rather than person to person",
    "Polio"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Clostridium tetani spores are ubiquitous in soil, so every individual must be individually immunised. This is why maternal immunisation is essential for preventing neonatal tetanus.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Tetanus",
   "tags": [
