   "topic": "Respiratory & vaccine-preventable disease epidemiology (measles, diphtheria, polio)",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Chickenpox is infectious from:",
   "options": [
    "Only during fever",
    "Only after crusting",
    "Two weeks before",
    "One to two days before the rash until all lesions crust"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "The rash is centripetal, appearing in successive crops so that lesions of different stages coexist - pleomorphism, which distinguishes it from smallpox where lesions were centrifugal and monomorphic.",
