   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "International health, WHO, SDGs & disaster management",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "The greatest public health priority in a refugee camp is:",
   "options": [
    "Safe water, sanitation, food, shelter and measles immunisation",
    "Surgical services",
    "Chronic disease care",
    "Dental care"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Measles vaccination with vitamin A is a top priority because overcrowding and malnutrition make measles outbreaks devastating, historically a major cause of camp mortality.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Disaster Management",
   "tags": [
    "#high-yield"
   ],
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_PSM_INT_010",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "International health, WHO, SDGs & disaster management",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Universal health coverage means that:",
   "options": [
    "All people receive needed quality health services without financial hardship",
    "Free care for all diseases",
    "Government provision only",
    "Insurance for the poor only"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Its three dimensions are population covered, services included and proportion of costs met. Reducing catastrophic out-of-pocket expenditure, which is very high in India, is central to it.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Health Care Delivery",
   "tags": [
