   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Diarrhoeal disease, enteric fever, hepatitis & helminths",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The chronic carrier state in typhoid is most often located in the:",
   "options": [
    "Gallbladder, especially in women with gallstones",
    "Kidney",
    "Spleen",
    "Bone marrow"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Chronic carriers excrete organisms for over a year and are a persisting source of infection, as illustrated by Typhoid Mary. Cholecystectomy may be needed when antibiotics fail.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Enteric Fever",
