   "part": "B",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Health planning, committees & health policy",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The National Rural Health Mission was launched in 2005 principally to:",
   "options": [
    "Improve rural health infrastructure and outcomes with community participation and flexible financing",
    "Build medical colleges",
    "Provide insurance",
    "Regulate drugs"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Key innovations were the ASHA, untied funds, Rogi Kalyan Samitis and village committees. It merged with the urban mission in 2013 to form the National Health Mission.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. National Health Mission",
   "tags": [
