   "topic": "Zoonoses: rabies, plague, leptospirosis, brucellosis",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "India accounts for a large share of global rabies deaths, with the principal reservoir being:",
   "options": [
    "Bats",
    "Cattle",
    "Rodents",
    "The stray dog"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Dog bites cause the overwhelming majority of human rabies in India. Mass dog vaccination achieving 70% coverage, alongside population management, is the only route to elimination.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Rabies",
   "tags": [
