   "topic": "Bleeding disorders, thrombophilia & anticoagulation",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "The commonest inherited thrombophilia in populations of European descent is:",
   "options": [
    "Factor V Leiden",
    "Antithrombin deficiency",
    "Protein C deficiency",
    "Prothrombin gene mutation"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "The point mutation makes factor Va resistant to cleavage by activated protein C; it is common but confers a far lower risk per carrier than the rarer antithrombin deficiency.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 65 (Disorders of Coagulation and Thrombosis)",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01",
