   "topic": "Bleeding disorders, thrombophilia & anticoagulation",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A prolonged APTT that fails to correct on mixing, with a history of recurrent miscarriage and thrombosis, indicates:",
   "options": [
    "Haemophilia A",
    "Antiphospholipid syndrome",
    "Von Willebrand disease",
    "Factor XIII deficiency"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Lupus anticoagulant interferes with phospholipid-dependent clotting in vitro but causes thrombosis in vivo, and diagnosis needs a positive test repeated after twelve weeks.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 65 (Disorders of Coagulation and Thrombosis)",
