   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The spirometric criterion for airflow obstruction in COPD is:",
   "options": [
    "FEV1 below 80 percent predicted alone",
    "Post-bronchodilator FEV1 to FVC ratio below 0.70",
    "FVC below 80 percent predicted",
    "Reduced total lung capacity"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "The fixed ratio after bronchodilator defines persistent obstruction, and the FEV1 percentage predicted is then used to grade severity rather than to make the diagnosis.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 286 (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease)",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_MED_CA_002",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Medicine",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The only interventions proven to slow decline and reduce mortality in COPD are:",
   "options": [
    "Mucolytics",
    "Inhaled corticosteroids",
    "Theophylline",
    "Smoking cessation and long-term oxygen in chronic hypoxaemia"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Bronchodilators improve symptoms and exacerbation rate but do not alter the slope of FEV1 decline, while stopping smoking and correcting sustained hypoxaemia do change survival.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 286 (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease)",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_MED_CA_003",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Medicine",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "Target oxygen saturation during an acute exacerbation of COPD is:",
   "options": [
    "88 to 92 percent",
    "94 to 98 percent",
    "Above 98 percent",
    "80 to 85 percent"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Excess oxygen worsens ventilation-perfusion matching and reduces hypoxic drive, precipitating carbon dioxide retention, so titration to a modest target is safer.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 286 (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease)",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_MED_CA_004",
