   "subject": "Medicine",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A young adult with emphysema affecting the lower zones and deranged liver enzymes should be tested for:",
   "options": [
    "Lymphangioleiomyomatosis",
    "Cystic fibrosis",
    "Sarcoidosis",
    "Alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Unopposed neutrophil elastase destroys basal lung tissue and the misfolded Z protein accumulates in hepatocytes, giving the combination of basal emphysema and liver disease.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. 286 (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease)",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_MED_CA_007",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Medicine",
   "source": "ai",
   "verified": "Y",
   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A fall in peak expiratory flow to below 50 percent of personal best with a silent chest indicates:",
   "options": [
    "Good control",
    "Moderate exacerbation",
    "Life-threatening acute severe asthma",
    "Vocal cord dysfunction"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Wheeze needs airflow to generate it, so a quiet chest with poor flows means airflow has almost ceased, and this patient needs urgent bronchodilators, systemic steroids and consideration of ventilation.",
