   "topic": "COPD & asthma",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A normal or rising PaCO2 in a patient with acute severe asthma signifies:",
   "options": [
    "Hyperventilation",
    "Adequate response to treatment",
    "Coexisting metabolic alkalosis",
    "Impending respiratory failure from fatigue"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Acute asthma normally causes hypocapnia from tachypnoea, so a normalising carbon dioxide means alveolar ventilation is falling as the patient tires and is an indication for critical care.",
