   "topic": "Cardiomyopathies & adult congenital heart disease",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "The commonest congenital heart defect surviving undetected into adulthood is:",
   "options": [
    "Transposition of the great arteries",
    "Ventricular septal defect",
    "Tetralogy of Fallot",
    "Atrial septal defect"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "The left-to-right shunt is low pressure and often silent for decades, presenting later with a fixed split second sound, atrial arrhythmias or pulmonary hypertension.",
