   "topic": "Tubulointerstitial disease, RTA & renal replacement therapy",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Which finding indicates that chronic kidney disease has caused secondary hyperparathyroidism with high-turnover bone disease?",
   "options": [
    "Low phosphate with low parathyroid hormone",
    "High phosphate, low calcitriol and a markedly raised parathyroid hormone",
    "Normal biochemistry with osteoporosis",
    "High calcium with low parathyroid hormone"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Reduced renal 1-alpha-hydroxylation lowers calcitriol while phosphate retention and FGF23 rise, together driving parathyroid hyperplasia; management is phosphate binders, active vitamin D analogues and calcimimetics.",
   "reference": "Harrison's Principles of Internal Medicine 21e, Ch. Chronic Kidney Disease",
