   "topic": "Abnormal labour: malpresentation, obstructed labour, CPD",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A woman in obstructed labour has a temperature of 39 degrees, a pulse of 130 and offensive liquor after 20 hours of labour at home. The most urgent priority alongside delivery is:",
   "options": [
    "Immediate forceps delivery",
    "Antibiotics and fluid resuscitation before operative intervention",
    "Oxytocin infusion",
    "Manual dilatation of the cervix"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Obstructed labour with sepsis and dehydration carries high maternal mortality, so resuscitation and broad-spectrum antibiotics run concurrently with arranging caesarean delivery.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. Abnormal Labour",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_OBG_ABL_014",
   "part": "B",
