   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Abnormal labour: malpresentation, obstructed labour, CPD",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A short primigravida has a fetus with an estimated weight of 3.8 kg and the head remains high with a poorly applied cervix after 3 hours in the active phase. This picture suggests:",
   "options": [
    "Hypotonic uterine inertia alone",
    "Cephalopelvic disproportion",
    "Cervical dystocia",
    "Precipitate labour"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Failure of descent with a high head and a poorly applied cervix despite adequate contractions in a small woman with a large fetus indicates disproportion, and trial of labour must be abandoned rather than augmented.",
   "reference": "DC Dutta's Textbook of Obstetrics 9e, Ch. Abnormal Labour",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
