   "topic": "Contraception",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A woman using the progestogen-only pill misses a tablet by 5 hours. The advice is:",
   "options": [
    "Take two tablets and continue",
    "No action is needed",
    "Stop the pill and start a new pack after the next period",
    "Take it at once and use additional precautions for 48 hours"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Traditional progestogen-only pills have only a 3-hour window, so a delay beyond that requires backup contraception; the desogestrel formulation allows a 12-hour window.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. Contraception",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_OBG_C_004",
