    "After the first normal period",
    "Immediately, on the day of the procedure",
    "After a negative pregnancy test at 6 weeks"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Ovulation can occur within 2 to 3 weeks of abortion, so immediate initiation gives no additional risk and avoids the high rate of rapid repeat pregnancy seen with delayed starts.",
   "reference": "Shaw's Textbook of Gynaecology 17e, Ch. Contraception",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
