   "stem": "A woman having oxytocin augmentation develops contractions lasting 90 seconds occurring six times in 10 minutes with a fetal bradycardia. The first action is:",
   "options": [
    "Perform immediate forceps delivery",
    "Increase the oxytocin to establish a regular pattern",
    "Stop the oxytocin, turn her to the left lateral position, give oxygen and consider a tocolytic",
    "Start magnesium sulphate"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Uterine hyperstimulation reduces placental perfusion during contraction, so removing the stimulus and improving uteroplacental flow is the immediate remedy before deciding on delivery.",
