   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A sputum sample for bacterial culture shows more than 25 squamous epithelial cells per low-power field. The correct action is:",
   "options": [
    "Reject the specimen as saliva and request a repeat, since it does not represent lower respiratory secretions",
    "Process it but report only anaerobes",
    "Culture it and report all isolates as pathogens",
    "Add it to blood culture broth"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Screening a Gram-stained smear for squamous cells and neutrophils before culture prevents reporting of upper airway commensals as pathogens. A good specimen shows abundant neutrophils with few squamous cells, and rejecting poor samples improves both the predictive value of the result and antibiotic decisions.",
   "reference": "Ananthanarayan and Paniker's Textbook of Microbiology 11e, Ch. Diagnostic Microbiology",
   "verify_note": "rewritten because the original stem duplicated Q_MIC_SPC_001 on blood culture collection (Jaccard 0.75); replaced with specimen quality assessment (plan 6.2)"
