   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A 9-month-old is treated for acute diarrhoea. For how long, and at what dose, should zinc be continued after the diarrhoea stops?",
   "options": [
    "14 days in total at 20 mg daily",
    "Only until the diarrhoea stops",
    "3 days at 10 mg daily",
    "6 weeks at 40 mg daily"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "The full 14-day course is what reduces recurrence over the following two to three months, and infants under 6 months receive 10 mg daily; stopping when stools settle loses most of the benefit.",
   "reference": "OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Diarrhoeal Diseases and Fluid Therapy",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_PED_DIA_013",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "Pediatrics",
