   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "A child with diarrhoea is restless and irritable with sunken eyes, drinks eagerly and has a skin pinch that goes back slowly. The classification and plan are:",
   "options": [
    "Some dehydration, treated with oral rehydration solution under supervision (Plan B)",
    "No dehydration, Plan A",
    "Severe dehydration, Plan C",
    "Severe malnutrition with shock"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Two or more of these signs define some dehydration, requiring about 75 mL per kg of oral rehydration solution over 4 hours with reassessment, whereas lethargy or inability to drink indicates severe dehydration.",
   "reference": "OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Diarrhoeal Diseases and Fluid Therapy",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01",
   "verify_note": "reviewed against a cross-topic duplicate candidate in the same subject; answer, topic and reference confirmed"
  },
