   "topic": "Fluid & electrolyte therapy and diarrhoeal disease in children",
   "difficulty": "H",
   "stem": "A child with diarrhoea develops seizures and a serum sodium of 160 mmol per litre. Correction must be gradual because:",
   "options": [
    "Sodium cannot be corrected orally",
    "Rapid correction causes osmotic demyelination",
    "Rapid lowering of sodium causes cerebral oedema as water shifts into brain cells that have accumulated osmolytes",
    "Seizures always require hypertonic saline"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "In hypernatraemia the brain accumulates idiogenic osmoles, so sodium is lowered by no more than 10 to 12 mmol per litre per day; osmotic demyelination is the hazard of correcting chronic hyponatraemia too fast.",
