    "Delayed in language",
    "Delayed in fine motor skills",
    "Advanced for age",
    "Appropriate for age across gross motor, fine motor, language and social domains"
   ],
   "correct": 3,
   "concept": "Copying a cross and hopping belong to 4 years, copying a square and a triangle to 4.5 and 5 years, and using a spoon well and pulling off shoes to 2 years, so mapping each skill to its domain and age is how delay is identified.",
   "reference": "OP Ghai Essential Pediatrics 9e, Ch. Growth and Development",
