   "topic": "Association & causation, bias, confounding, measures of risk",
   "difficulty": "E",
   "stem": "In a cohort study, the incidence of lung cancer is 40 per 1000 in smokers and 8 per 1000 in non-smokers. The relative risk is:",
   "options": [
    "5",
    "32",
    "0.2",
    "48"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Relative risk is the incidence in the exposed divided by the incidence in the unexposed, so 40 divided by 8 gives 5, meaning smokers have five times the risk; the attributable risk of 32 per 1000 gives the excess burden.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Epidemiology",
   "verified_on": "2026-09-01",
   "verify_note": "reviewed against a concept-similarity duplicate candidate; answer, topic and reference confirmed"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q_PSM_ACB_002",
   "part": "B",
   "subject": "PSM (Community Medicine)",
