   "stem": "Which measure of association is obtained from a case-control study?",
   "options": [
    "Incidence rate",
    "Relative risk",
    "Odds ratio",
    "Attributable risk"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Because subjects are selected on outcome, incidence cannot be measured, so exposure odds are compared; the odds ratio approximates the relative risk when the disease is rare.",
   "reference": "Park's Textbook of Preventive and Social Medicine 27e, Ch. Epidemiology",
