   "topic": "Association & causation, bias, confounding, measures of risk",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A study of diet and cancer asks participants to recall their intake from twenty years earlier, and cases remember differently from controls. Which bias is this, and to which design is it most specific?",
   "options": [
    "Recall bias, a form of information bias particularly affecting case-control studies",
    "Selection bias, specific to cohort studies",
    "Confounding, which recall cannot produce",
    "Lead time bias, specific to screening"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Selection bias arises from how participants enter a study and information bias from how data are obtained after entry, and recall bias is reduced by using records rather than memory or by blinding interviewers to case status.",
