    "Herd immunity, implying no further action is needed",
    "The iceberg phenomenon, implying that control based only on notified cases will fail",
    "Secular trend, implying a long-term decline"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Subclinical infections, carriers and undiagnosed cases greatly outnumber the clinical cases that come to notice, which is why serological surveys and surveillance rather than case counts alone guide policy.",
