   "topic": "Anxiety disorders & substance use",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Two months after surviving a bus accident a man has intrusive re-experiencing, nightmares, avoidance of travel and hypervigilance. What is the diagnosis and the first-line treatment?",
   "options": [
    "Post-traumatic stress disorder, treated with trauma-focused cognitive behaviour therapy and a serotonergic antidepressant",
    "Acute stress reaction, treated with a benzodiazepine",
    "Adjustment disorder, treated with reassurance alone",
    "Dissociative amnesia, treated with hypnosis"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "An acute stress reaction resolves within days and adjustment disorder lacks the re-experiencing, and routine benzodiazepines are avoided because they impair the emotional processing that recovery depends on.",
