   "topic": "Anxiety disorders & substance use",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A patient on alprazolam for 8 months needs increasing doses and becomes tremulous and anxious when a dose is missed. How should this be managed and what is the role of flumazenil?",
   "options": [
    "Substitute a long-acting benzodiazepine such as diazepam and taper it slowly; flumazenil is reserved for acute overdose and may precipitate seizures in a dependent patient",
