   "topic": "Child psychiatry, psychopharmacology, ECT & psychotherapies",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "How many sessions does a typical course of electroconvulsive therapy involve, and what is its principal adverse effect?",
   "options": [
    "A single session, with permanent memory loss",
    "About 6 to 12 sessions given two or three times a week, with transient anterograde and retrograde memory impairment as the main adverse effect",
    "Daily sessions for 3 months, with hepatotoxicity",
    "Two sessions, with tardive dyskinesia"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "It is the fastest effective treatment for severe depression with suicidal risk, catatonia or refusal to eat, and unilateral electrode placement and brief pulse stimuli reduce the cognitive effects.",
