   "topic": "Child psychiatry, psychopharmacology, ECT & psychotherapies",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Which feature distinguishes conduct disorder from oppositional defiant disorder?",
   "options": [
    "Conduct disorder involves violation of the rights of others or major social norms such as theft, cruelty and assault, whereas oppositional defiant disorder involves defiance, irritability and argumentativeness without such violation",
    "Both require criminal acts",
    "Oppositional defiant disorder involves cruelty to animals",
    "Conduct disorder occurs only after 18 years"
   ],
   "correct": 0,
   "concept": "Management in both rests on parent management training and family intervention rather than medication, and conduct disorder in childhood is the strongest predictor of antisocial personality disorder in adult life.",
