   "verified_by": "model-audit",
   "topic": "Delirium, dementia & organic mental disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "Which measures reduce the incidence of delirium in a hospitalised elderly patient?",
   "options": [
    "Physical restraint at night",
    "Routine prophylactic haloperidol",
    "Reorientation, correction of sensory deficits with spectacles and hearing aids, early mobilisation, sleep hygiene, hydration and review of culprit drugs",
    "Routine sedation to ensure sleep"
   ],
   "correct": 2,
   "concept": "Antipsychotics have no established preventive role and restraint worsens agitation and injury, so the evidence supports the multicomponent non-pharmacological bundle rather than any drug.",
