   "topic": "Somatoform, dissociative, personality & sexual disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "How is somatic symptom disorder distinguished from factitious disorder and from malingering?",
   "options": [
    "All three involve conscious production",
    "In somatic symptom disorder the symptoms are genuinely experienced without conscious production, in factitious disorder they are deliberately produced for the sick role, and in malingering they are feigned for an external gain",
    "Somatic symptom disorder involves conscious feigning",
    "Malingering is a psychiatric diagnosis with the sick role as its motive"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Malingering is not classified as a mental disorder at all because the motive is external, so distinguishing motive rather than the symptom itself is what determines both diagnosis and management.",
