   "topic": "Somatoform, dissociative, personality & sexual disorders",
   "difficulty": "M",
   "stem": "A young man is preoccupied for hours daily with a barely perceptible defect in his nose, seeks repeated cosmetic surgery and avoids social contact. What is the diagnosis and the treatment?",
   "options": [
    "Delusional disorder, treated with an antipsychotic alone",
    "Body dysmorphic disorder, treated with a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor and cognitive behaviour therapy rather than surgery",
    "Somatic symptom disorder, treated with reassurance",
    "Social anxiety disorder, treated with a beta blocker"
   ],
   "correct": 1,
   "concept": "Surgery characteristically fails to satisfy the patient and the preoccupation shifts to another feature, and the suicide risk in this disorder is high enough to warrant specific enquiry.",
